// front::emit: smith's own emitter (#1119, B1 of #1112): a typed syntax tree (front::ast) in, an LLVM module out,
// through LLVM's C API (`c::LLVM...`) only. Modules are never turned into C. Internal: not wired into `smith cc`, and
// its concept (knowledge/) comes with J2.
//
// WHAT IT EMITS TODAY (B1): functions with a body, parameters and a result of `I8 I16 I32 I64 U8 U16 U32 U64 char
// Bool`; blocks, `return value;`, locals (`I32 t = a * b;`, `auto t = ...`); integer literals, names, unary `- + ~`,
// binary
// `+ - * / % << >> & ^ |`, assignment, plain and compound. Signed overflow, division by zero, `MIN / -1` and bad shift
// amounts are checks in every build (`llvm.*.with.overflow`, `llvm.trap`); unsigned arithmetic wraps. Everything else
// is an `Error` naming the node, with its span ("not emitted yet: while"); no node makes a crash. The first problem
// stops the walk and the half-built module is disposed of.
//
// THE FILES. emit.smith (this file) has the entry point, the walk and its dispatch over every kind of Stmt and Expr,
// the type mapping and the two passes. emit_state.smith has the types they share (a module cannot import one that
// imports it: the handlers need the state, and this file needs the handlers). emit_arith.smith is B1's expressions.
// The others are stubs with their handlers' final signatures, each returning `not emitted yet`, and the ticket that
// owns it fills the bodies and never edits this file: emit_control (B2: if, loops, switch, goto, defer, comparisons,
// `&&`, `||`, `!`, `?:`, `true`), emit_call (B3a: calls, `return;`, prototypes), emit_memory (B3b: `&`, `*`, index,
// member, compound literals, casts, `null`, sizeof and friends, pointer/array/record types, records, globals),
// emit_debug (B5: called at fixed points whether or not debug info is on; doing nothing is success). emit_jit is the
// test helper (LLJIT). The tests are tests/front_emit_*_test.smith.
//
// FLOATS (#1617): `f32`/`f64` (`F32`/`F64`), and `f16`/`bf16` (#1629: LLVM `half` and `bfloat`) are `floating` types
// made by emit_arith::type_float. Literals, `+ - * /`, unary `-`, ordered comparisons (`!=` unordered), `f32` to `f64`
// and integer to float conversions, and casts go to emit_arith.
//
// SLICES (#1623): `[]T` and `str` are the literal struct `{ ptr, usize }` (emit_memory::type_slice). String literals,
// `xs[a:b]` and `s[i]` go to emit_memory; an array that is a place, where a slice is expected, becomes `{ address, N }`
// (`is_array_place`, aliasing the array), and an array value is stored in a slot (`convert_value`).
//
// ARRAYS (#1624): `[1, 2]` goes to emit_memory::array_literal, or to emit_vector::list for a vector.
//
// WAVE 3 (#1582 of #1428) added one stub per new area, the same way: emit_option (`?T`, `.some`, `.none`, `if let`;
// #1584), emit_match (enumerations, `.red`, `match`; #1585), emit_value (an `if` or a block as a value), emit_iter
// (`for x in xs`; #1586), emit_tuple and emit_lambda (the next batch). This file routes to them and nothing else will
// change in it. The hooks `state::type_of`, `state::type_of_node` and `state::convert` let a handler reach what lives
// here without importing this file (a cycle).
//
// THE PASSES. `emit::module` makes the module, sets its triple and data layout from `Options.target` (it never asks
// the host), then (1) declares every record, then (2) every function with its symbol and type (and every global), so
// that a call finds any function whatever the order, then (3) emits the bodies. A function's LLVM name is its module's
// path and its name joined by `::` (`front::test::add`), the label the generated headers give, unless the function has
// `@c_name("x")` (then `x`) or is `main` (then `main`); `pub`, exported, a c_name and `main` are external linkage, the
// rest internal. `@inline`, `@noinline` and `@cold` (or `[[std::...]]`) are LLVM attributes. The last line of a body
// that is an expression is its value, `let _ = f()` drops the value, and a local `const X = v` is a constant slot. At
// the end it runs the verifier; its message becomes an `Error`.
//
// THE WALK has no recursion (a compile error in a module): an explicit work stack and a value stack, both in the
// `Emitter` (emit_state.smith, with every field the later tickets need; one that is missing is an escalation, not an
// edit). The protocol, which B2, B3a and B3b build on:
//
//  1. A `Work` item is one of four kinds, a payload enum. `eval` (an `Expr` and a `Hint`): its handler pushes exactly
//     ONE `Value` on the value stack. `place` (an `Expr`): its handler pushes ONE `Value` whose `llvm` is the ADDRESS
//     and `ty` the type stored there. `statement` (a `Stmt`): its handler pushes nothing. `then` (a `Then`: a function
//     and the data the pusher stored in it): a continuation, called as `item.run(e, &item)`.
//  2. The stack runs LIFO. A handler does its work now, or pushes more work: to evaluate `a` then `b` and then combine
//     them it pushes the continuation `combine` first, then `eval b`, then `eval a`. The continuation finds `b`'s value
//     on top of the value stack, then `a`'s (`state::pop_value`), and pushes its own. A handler that needs `a`'s value
//     before it knows how to evaluate `b` pushes a continuation that peeks at it (`state::peek_value`), as the binary
//     operators do for the type of the right side. Values are never left behind: what a handler or continuation pushes
//     is exactly its one Value; a statement leaves the value stack as it found it.
//  3. A `Hint` is the type a literal takes where it stands (the other operand's, the variable's, the function's
//     result). `state::no_hint()` when there is none; an integer literal then is an `I32`.
//  4. Handlers: `Status f(Emitter *e, const ast::Expr *x, Hint hint)` for an expression, `Status f(Emitter *e, const
//     ast::Stmt *s)` for a statement, `Status f(Emitter *e, const ast::Expr *x)` for a place, `Status f(Emitter *e,
//     const Then *w)` for a continuation. Status is a Result: `try` passes a failure up, `state::success()` is success,
//     `state::fail(message, span)` and `state::not_emitted(kind, span)` fail. A failure ends the walk at once; the
//     work and value stacks are dropped, so a handler needs no cleanup of them.
//  5. Code goes through `e->builder`. A handler that makes blocks leaves the builder positioned in the block where the
//     code goes on. A statement that finds the block already ended (after a `return`) is emitted into a fresh block
//     no one jumps to, so the IR stays valid. Allocas go through `state::new_alloca`, which puts them in the entry
//     block. Locals are `Local`s in `e->locals`, scopes bracket them (`state::begin_scope`, `end_scope`).
//  6. Hooks B2 fills: `emit_control::end_of_block` (runs when a block ends, before its locals go) and
//     `emit_control::before_return` (before `ret`): the pending `defer`s run there. A hook may push work: it runs
//     before the scope closes or the `ret` is built (the closing and the `ret` are continuations pushed first).
//  7. Writing handlers in today's smith (issue #1153): dispatch on a node's kind with a chain of `if (x->kind ==
//     .name)`, never `switch`/`case`, in a file that imports front::ast: a `case .name:` label spells an export of
//     front::ast, so the compiler reads ast's function bodies, which do not compile. Read the payload fields you need
//     (`x->kind.call.args`) into locals right after testing the kind and before any call that is passed the node:
//     `smith-enum` forgets the kind at such a call. A test that runs the emitter or the JIT must not have an arena set
//     as the current allocator (LLVM allocates with `malloc` and keeps some of it between tests): see emit_jit.smith.
//  8. A type is a `Ty` (the LLVM type and what it does not say: signedness, name, element). A pointer type is made in
//     one place, `state::pointer_type`, which takes an address space. Sizes and alignments come from the data layout
//     (`e->target_data`), never from the host. A handler that needs a type calls `emit::type_of`.
module front::emit;

import front::ast;
import front::emit_aggregate as aggregates;
import front::eval;
import front::emit_arith as arith;
import front::emit_builtin as builtin;
import front::emit_call as call;
import front::emit_control as control;
import front::emit_debug as debug;
import front::emit_iter as looping;
import front::emit_lambda as lambdas;
import front::emit_match as matching;
import front::emit_memory;
import front::emit_option as optional;
import front::emit_record as records;
import front::emit_state as state;
import front::emit_stream as streams;
import front::emit_tuple as tupled;
import front::emit_value as blockval;
import front::emit_vector as vectors;
import front::types;
import front::types_stream;
import std::format;
import std::arena;
import std::mem;
import <llvm-c/Analysis.h>;
import <llvm-c/Core.h>;
import <llvm-c/Target.h>;

export typedef state::Error Error;
export typedef state::Target Target;
export typedef state::Options Options;
export typedef Result(c::LLVMModuleRef, state::Error) ModuleResult;

// What `module_all` gives: the module, or (module null) every error, in the order found (#2982).
export struct Emitted {
    c::LLVMModuleRef module;
    state::Error errors[:];
};

// Give back a string of the allocator in force (an Error's message) when the caller is done with it.
export void free_text(Str text) {
    state::free_text(text);
}

export void free_error(state::Error error) {
    state::free_text(error.message);
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Types

// `Void`: an LLVM `void`, kind `integer`, zero bits, named `Void`. Only a function's result and a call's value have it.
static state::Ty void_type(state::Emitter *e) {
    state::Ty none = {.kind = {.integer = {}}, .llvm = c::LLVMVoidTypeInContext(e->context), .name = "Void"};
    return none;
}

export state::TyResult type_of_checked(state::Emitter *e, types::TypeRef t, ast::Span span);

// `c::point` written as a type: what the header named it, as the checker typed it (#1762).
static state::TyResult type_of_header(state::Emitter *e, const ast::TypeExpr *t) {
    if (t->kind != .named || e->options.checked == nullptr) return state::ty_fail("not a C type", t->span);
    ast::Path path = t->kind.named.path;
    Str full = state::msg(format::push("c::", path.segments[1].text));
    const types::Symbol *symbol =
        types::lookup_as(&e->options.checked->scopes, full, true); // a tag over a function (#2610)
    state::free_text(full);
    if (symbol == nullptr || symbol->kind != .type_name) return state::ty_fail("unknown C type", t->span);
    return type_of_checked(e, symbol->type, t->span);
}

// `let Plain = fn(u64) -> u64`: a name for a type, which the checker declared as that type (#2190).
static Bool is_alias_symbol(const types::Symbol *s) {
    return s != nullptr && s->kind == .type_name && s->decl != nullptr && s->decl->kind == .variable;
}

// The alias's written type, emitted as any written type is (a function type has no checker form to emit yet).
static state::TyResult type_of_alias(state::Emitter *e, const types::Symbol *s) {
    const ast::Expr *init = s->decl->kind == .variable ? s->decl->kind.variable.init : nullptr;
    // `const Pair = (i32, f32)`: a tuple of names has no written type; the checker made its type.
    if (init != nullptr && init->kind == .tuple_lit) return type_of_checked(e, s->type, s->decl->span);
    // `let Allocator = c.SmithAllocator`: a name for a type of a C header; the checker made its type.
    if (init != nullptr && init->kind == .name && countof(init->kind.name.path.segments) == 1) {
        // `Wide := u128`: a name for a built-in type, emitted as that type is written
        ast::TypeExpr *written = ast::make_type({.named = {.path = init->kind.name.path}});
        written->span = s->decl->span;
        return state::type_of(e, written);
    }
    if (init != nullptr && (init->kind == .member || init->kind == .name || init->kind == .call))
        return type_of_checked(e, s->type, s->decl->span); // also `IntPair := Pair(i32)`
    if (init == nullptr || init->kind != .type_value) return state::ty_fail("unknown type", s->decl->span);
    // `Edits := []mut Edit` of front::parse, used from another module: `Edit` is read in front::parse's scope, as an
    // imported record's fields are (#2984; read in the user's scope it was unknown, and before that a loop).
    Str prefix = emit_memory::record_module_prefix(s->name);
    if (countof(prefix) == 0) return state::type_of(e, init->kind.type_value.type);
    Str outer = e->import_scope;
    e->import_scope = prefix;
    state::TyResult made = state::type_of(e, init->kind.type_value.type); // the hook: no recursion here
    e->import_scope = outer;
    return made;
}

// An enumeration of an imported module (`ast.ExprKind`, or `ExprKind` inside a record of front::ast), declared when the
// first use needs it, its payload types read in that module's scope. False for any other symbol.
static Bool is_enum_symbol(const types::Symbol *target) {
    return target != nullptr && target->kind == .type_name && target->decl != nullptr &&
           target->decl->kind == .enumeration;
}

static state::TyResult imported_enum(state::Emitter *e, const types::Symbol *target) {
    if (target->decl->kind != .enumeration) return state::ty_fail("unknown type", target->decl->span);
    Str bare = target->decl->kind.enumeration.name;
    state::Ty ty = {};
    if (!matching::type_enum(e, bare, &ty)) {
        Str outer = e->import_scope;
        e->import_scope = emit_memory::record_module_prefix(types::name_of(target->type));
        state::Status declared = matching::enum_decl(e, target->decl);
        Str scope = e->import_scope;
        e->import_scope = outer;
        declared = state::in_module(declared, scope);
        if (declared == .error) return {.error = declared.error};
        matching::type_enum(e, bare, &ty);
    }
    return ty;
}

// `v.Vec`, a record of an imported module: `v` is the module's alias, and the checker declared the record under the
// module's path (`geom::vec::Vec`).
static state::TyResult type_of_imported(state::Emitter *e, const ast::TypeExpr *t) {
    if (t->kind != .named || e->options.checked == nullptr)
        return state::ty_fail("not emitted yet: qualified type", t->span);
    ast::Path path = t->kind.named.path;
    const types::Scopes *scopes = &e->options.checked->scopes;
    const types::Symbol *module = types::lookup(scopes, path.segments[0].text);
    // `format.Written` in the signature or the body of an imported module's function or generic instance: the module
    // is one that module imported, found under its path
    if (module == nullptr && (countof(e->import_scope) > 0 || countof(e->instance_scope) > 0)) {
        Str base = countof(e->import_scope) > 0 ? e->import_scope : e->instance_scope;
        Str own = state::msg(format::push(base, path.segments[0].text));
        module = types::lookup(scopes, own);
        state::free_text(own);
    }
    if (module == nullptr || module->kind != .module_name || module->decl->kind != .import_module)
        return state::ty_fail("unknown module", path.segments[0].span);
    ast::Path via = module->decl->kind.import_module.path;
    Str full = state::msg(format::push(path.segments[1].text));
    for (Usize i = countof(via.segments); i > 0; i--) {
        Str longer = state::msg(format::push(via.segments[i - 1].text, "::", full));
        state::free_text(full);
        full = longer;
    }
    const types::Symbol *target = types::lookup(scopes, full);
    state::free_text(full);
    if (is_alias_symbol(target)) return type_of_alias(e, target);
    if (is_enum_symbol(target)) return imported_enum(e, target);
    if (target == nullptr || target->kind != .type_name || target->decl == nullptr || target->decl->kind != .record)
        return state::ty_fail("unknown type", t->span);
    return emit_memory::imported_record(e, target->decl, types::name_of(target->type));
}

// A record named by its bare name inside an imported function's signature (`fn dot(a: Vec, ...)` of `geom::vec`): the
// record of that module, declared as `type_of_imported` declares one. False for any other name.
static Bool type_in_import_scope(state::Emitter *e, ast::Path path, state::TyResult *made) {
    Str full = state::msg(format::push(e->import_scope, path.segments[0].text));
    const types::Symbol *target = types::lookup(&e->options.checked->scopes, full);
    state::free_text(full);
    if (is_alias_symbol(target)) {
        *made = type_of_alias(e, target);
        return true;
    }
    if (is_enum_symbol(target)) {
        *made = imported_enum(e, target);
        return true;
    }
    if (target == nullptr || target->kind != .type_name || target->decl == nullptr || target->decl->kind != .record)
        return false;
    *made = emit_memory::imported_record(e, target->decl, types::name_of(target->type));
    return true;
}

static state::TyResult ok_ty(state::Ty ty) {
    return ty;
}

// `typeof(v)`: the type of the local `v`, else the type the checker gave the operand (in a generic body, of the
// instance being emitted) (#2648). False when `t` is no `typeof` or nothing types it.
static Bool type_of_typeof(state::Emitter *e, const ast::TypeExpr *t, state::TyResult *made) {
    if (t->kind != .type_of) return false;
    const ast::Expr *operand = t->kind.type_of.operand;
    state::Local local = {};
    if (operand->kind == .name && countof(operand->kind.name.path.segments) == 1 &&
        state::find_local(e, operand->kind.name.path.segments[0].text, &local)) {
        state::TyResult found = ok_ty(local.ty);
        *made = found;
        return true;
    }
    if (e->options.checked == nullptr) return false;
    types::TypeRef typed = types::type_of(e->options.checked, operand);
    if (typed == nullptr || typed == e->options.checked->table.invalid) return false;
    *made = type_of_checked(e, typed, t->span);
    return true;
}

// An applied type other than an option or a result: `Lambda(bool (i32))` and `Fn(...)` are the fn value of their
// function type, as the checker types them (#3036); `vec(T, N)` is a vector.
static state::TyResult type_applied(state::Emitter *e, const ast::TypeExpr *t) {
    if (t->kind != .applied) return state::ty_fail("not an applied type", t->span);
    ast::Path applied = t->kind.applied.name;
    ast::TypeArg args[:] = t->kind.applied.args;
    Bool lambda = countof(applied.segments) == 1 && (state::same_text(applied.segments[0].text, "Lambda") ||
                                                     state::same_text(applied.segments[0].text, "Fn"));
    if (lambda && countof(args) == 1) {
        const ast::TypeArg *only = &args[0];
        if (*only == .type && only->type.type->kind == .function) return lambdas::type_function(e, only->type.type);
    }
    // a type function's (`Pair(i32)`, `widen(T)`): the type the checker computed for this place
    types::TypeRef held = nullptr;
    if (e->options.checked != nullptr) held = types::applied_type(e->options.checked, t, state::instance_number(e));
    if (held != nullptr) return type_of_checked(e, held, t->span);
    if (countof(applied.segments) != 1 || !state::same_text(applied.segments[0].text, "vec"))
        return state::ty_fail_with(t->span, "not emitted yet: the applied type `",
                                   applied.segments[countof(applied.segments) - 1].text, "`");
    return vectors::type_vector(e, t);
}

// A one-name type that a name in force stands for: a bound type parameter, `W` after `W := widen(T)`, or `Element`
// after `const Element = typeof(xs[0])`.
static Bool type_of_local(state::Emitter *e, const ast::TypeExpr *t, Str name, state::TyResult *out) {
    types::TypeRef bound = nullptr;
    if (state::bound_type(e, name, &bound)) {
        *out = type_of_checked(e, bound, t->span);
        return true;
    }
    types::TypeRef made = state::local_made(e, name);
    if (made != nullptr) {
        *out = type_of_checked(e, made, t->span);
        return true;
    }
    const ast::TypeExpr *held = state::local_type(e, name);
    if (held == nullptr) return false;
    *out = state::type_of(e, held);
    return true;
}

// The LLVM type of a type expression.
export state::TyResult type_of(state::Emitter *e, const ast::TypeExpr *t) {
    // Chains of `if`, not a `switch`: a `case` label that spells the name of one of front::ast's functions (`named`,
    // `name`, `integer`, ...) makes the compiler read that module's function bodies, which today fail to compile.
    if (t->kind == .named) {
        ast::Path path = t->kind.named.path;
        state::Ty ty = {};
        if (countof(path.segments) == 2 && state::same_text(path.segments[0].text, "c")) return type_of_header(e, t);
        if (countof(path.segments) == 2 && e->options.checked != nullptr &&
            types::header_binding_in(e->options.checked, path.segments[0].text, e->instance_scope) != nullptr)
            return type_of_header(e, t); // `stdio.size_t` is the header's `c::size_t`
        if (countof(path.segments) == 2) return type_of_imported(e, t);
        state::TyResult local = {};
        if (countof(path.segments) == 1 && type_of_local(e, t, path.segments[0].text, &local)) return local;
        if (countof(path.segments) == 1 && state::scalar_type(e, path.segments[0].text, &ty)) return ty;
        if (countof(path.segments) == 1 && arith::type_float(e, path.segments[0].text, &ty)) return ty;
        if (countof(path.segments) == 1 && state::same_text(path.segments[0].text, "Void")) return void_type(e);
        if (countof(path.segments) == 1 && matching::type_enum(e, path.segments[0].text, &ty)) return ty;
        if (countof(path.segments) == 1 &&
            (state::same_text(path.segments[0].text, "str") || state::same_text(path.segments[0].text, "Str")))
            return emit_memory::type_slice(e, t);
        state::TyResult scoped = {};
        if (countof(path.segments) == 1 && countof(e->import_scope) > 0 && type_in_import_scope(e, path, &scoped))
            return scoped;
        if (countof(path.segments) == 1 && e->options.checked != nullptr) {
            const types::Symbol *alias = types::lookup(&e->options.checked->scopes, path.segments[0].text);
            if (is_alias_symbol(alias)) return type_of_alias(e, alias);
        }
        return emit_memory::type_record(e, t);
    }
    if (t->kind == .slice) return emit_memory::type_slice(e, t);
    if (t->kind == .block_type) return emit_memory::type_block(e, t);
    if (t->kind == .option) return optional::type_option(e, t);
    if (t->kind == .tuple) return tupled::type_tuple(e, t);
    if (t->kind == .record) return records::type_record(e, t);
    if (t->kind == .function) return lambdas::type_function(e, t);
    if (t->kind == .pointer) {
        // `*Word` with `let Word = c.uint32_t`: the checker's alias, emitted as the type it names
        const ast::TypeExpr *pointee = t->kind.pointer.pointee;
        state::TyResult scoped = {};
        if (pointee->kind == .named && countof(pointee->kind.named.path.segments) == 1 &&
            e->options.checked != nullptr && countof(e->import_scope) > 0 &&
            type_in_import_scope(e, pointee->kind.named.path, &scoped)) {
            // `*Tap` in a record of an imported module: that module's record, declared when first needed
            if (scoped == .error) return scoped;
            state::Ty made = emit_memory::pointer_over(e, scoped.ok);
            return made;
        }
        if (pointee->kind == .named && countof(pointee->kind.named.path.segments) == 1 &&
            e->options.checked != nullptr) {
            const types::Symbol *alias =
                types::lookup(&e->options.checked->scopes, pointee->kind.named.path.segments[0].text);
            if (is_alias_symbol(alias)) {
                state::TyResult inner = type_of_alias(e, alias);
                if (inner == .error) return inner;
                state::Ty made = emit_memory::pointer_over(e, inner.ok);
                return made;
            }
        }
        return emit_memory::type_pointer(e, t);
    }
    if (t->kind == .array) return emit_memory::type_array(e, t);
    if (streams::is_stream_type(t)) return streams::type_stream(e, t);
    if (optional::is_applied(t)) return optional::type_applied(e, t);
    if (t->kind == .applied) return type_applied(e, t);
    if (t->kind == .auto_type) return state::ty_fail("`auto` where a type is needed", t->span);
    state::TyResult typed = {};
    if (type_of_typeof(e, t, &typed)) return typed;
    return state::ty_fail_with(t->span, "not emitted yet: a type of kind `", state::type_kind_name(t), "`");
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The dispatch over every kind

static state::Status dispatch_unary(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Expr *x, ast::UnaryOp op, state::Hint hint) {
    switch (op) {
    case .negate:
    case .plus:
    case .bit_not:
        return arith::unary_op(e, x, hint);
    case .logical_not:
        return control::logical_not(e, x, hint);
    case .address_of:
        return emit_memory::address_of(e, x, hint);
    case .dereference:
        return emit_memory::dereference(e, x, hint);
    case .pre_increment:
    case .pre_decrement:
    case .post_increment:
    case .post_decrement:
        return arith::increment(e, x);
    }
}

// Whether the checker typed `x` as `f32` or `f64` (false with no checker result).
static Bool checked_floating(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Expr *x) {
    if (e->options.checked == nullptr) return false;
    types::TypeRef t = types::type_of(e->options.checked, x);
    return t != nullptr && t->kind == .floating;
}

// Whether the checker typed `x` as a vector (false with no checker result).
static Bool checked_vector(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Expr *x) {
    if (e->options.checked == nullptr) return false;
    types::TypeRef t = types::type_of(e->options.checked, x);
    return t != nullptr && t->kind == .vector;
}

static state::Status dispatch_binary(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Expr *x, ast::BinaryOp op, state::Hint hint) {
    if (x->kind == .binary && (checked_vector(e, x->kind.binary.left) || checked_vector(e, x->kind.binary.right)))
        return vectors::binary(e, x);
    switch (op) {
    case .add:
    case .subtract:
    case .multiply:
    case .divide:
    case .remainder:
    case .shift_left:
    case .shift_right:
    case .bit_and:
    case .bit_xor:
    case .bit_or:
        return arith::binary_op(e, x, hint);
    case .less:
    case .greater:
    case .less_equal:
    case .greater_equal:
    case .equal:
    case .not_equal:
        if (x->kind == .binary && checked_floating(e, x->kind.binary.left)) return arith::float_comparison(e, x, hint);
        return control::comparison(e, x, hint);
    case .logical_and:
    case .logical_or:
        return control::logical(e, x, hint);
    }
}

// A character literal is a `Char` (8 bits, unsigned) whatever the hint says; escapes were decoded by the parser.
static state::Status character_literal(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Expr *x) {
    if (x->kind != .character) {
        return state::fail("not a character literal", x->span);
    }
    state::Ty ty = {};
    state::scalar_type(e, "Char", &ty);
    U64 value = x->kind.character.value;
    if (value > 255) return state::failf(x->span, "character literal ", value, " does not fit char");
    state::push_value(e, (state::Value){.llvm = c::LLVMConstInt(ty.llvm, value, 0), .ty = ty});
    return state::success();
}

// `t.0` (a member whose name starts with a digit) or `t.count` on a named tuple the checker typed.
static Bool is_tuple_member(const state::Emitter *e, const ast::Expr *x) {
    if (x->kind != .member) return false;
    Str name = x->kind.member.name;
    if (countof(name) > 0 && name[0] >= '0' && name[0] <= '9') return true;
    if (e->options.checked == nullptr || x->kind.member.arrow) return false;
    types::TypeRef base = types::type_of(e->options.checked, x->kind.member.base);
    return base != nullptr && base->kind == .tuple;
}

// Whether the checker typed `x` as an option (false with no checker result).
static Bool checked_option(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Expr *x) {
    if (e->options.checked == nullptr) return false;
    types::TypeRef t = types::type_of(e->options.checked, x);
    return t != nullptr && (t->kind == .option || t->kind == .result_type);
}

// `.some(x)` and `.none` when an option is expected, `.red` otherwise.
static state::Status dispatch_variant(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Expr *x, state::Hint hint) {
    if ((hint.present && (hint.ty.kind == .option || hint.ty.kind == .result)) || checked_option(e, x))
        return optional::variant(e, x, hint);
    return matching::variant(e, x, hint);
}

// Whether `x` is a place (a name, a member, an index, `p.*`) the checker typed as a fixed array: where a slice is
// expected it is passed as `{ address, N }`, aliasing the array.
static Bool is_array_place(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Expr *x) {
    Bool place = x->kind == .name || x->kind == .member || x->kind == .index;
    place = place || (x->kind == .unary && x->kind.unary.op == .dereference);
    if (!place || e->options.checked == nullptr) return false;
    types::TypeRef t = types::type_of(e->options.checked, x);
    return t != nullptr && t->kind == .array;
}

// An `if`, `match` or block used as a value.
static state::Status dispatch_stmt_expr(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Expr *x, state::Hint hint) {
    if (x->kind != .stmt_expr) {
        return state::fail("not a statement used as a value", x->span);
    }
    const ast::Stmt *inner = x->kind.stmt_expr.stmt;
    if (inner->kind == .match_stmt) return matching::value_of(e, inner, hint);
    return blockval::value_of(e, inner, hint);
}

// `c::EOF`, `c::O_RDONLY`: a constant a header declared (an enumerator, a macro with a value, a `static const`),
// emitted where it is used as its initializer, typed as the checker typed it (#1762). Null when `x` is no such name.
static const ast::Expr *c_constant(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Expr *x) {
    if (e->options.checked == nullptr) return nullptr;
    Str full = "";
    if (x->kind == .member) { // `stdio.name` after `import c <stdio.h>` (#1678), unless a local hides the binding
        state::Local local = {};
        Str name = types::c_member_name_in(e->options.checked, x, e->instance_scope); // an instance: its module's
        if (countof(name) == 0 || state::find_local(e, types::c_member_base(x), &local)) return nullptr;
        full = state::msg(format::push("c::", name));
    } else if (x->kind == .name) {
        ast::Path path = x->kind.name.path;
        if (countof(path.segments) != 2 || !state::same_text(path.segments[0].text, "c")) return nullptr;
        full = state::msg(format::push("c::", path.segments[1].text));
    } else {
        return nullptr;
    }
    const types::Symbol *symbol = types::lookup(&e->options.checked->scopes, full);
    state::free_text(full);
    if (symbol == nullptr || symbol->kind != .variable || symbol->decl == nullptr || !symbol->decl->from_c)
        return nullptr;
    if (symbol->decl->kind != .variable) return nullptr;
    return symbol->decl->kind.variable.init;
}

// The names of `autodiff::out` (a path) or `autodiff.out` (a chain of `.`), the module first; none for anything else.
static types::Names qualified_names(const ast::Expr *x) {
    types::Names names = {};
    if (x->kind == .member) return types::member_names(x);
    if (x->kind != .name) return names;
    ast::Path path = x->kind.name.path;
    if (countof(path.segments) < 2 || countof(path.segments) > 8) return names;
    for (Usize i = 0; i < countof(path.segments); i++)
        names.items[i] = path.segments[i].text;
    names.count = countof(path.segments);
    return names;
}

// A bare name in the body of a generic's instance from another module: a global of that module, found under its prefix
// (`std::test::op_equal`) when no local of the body has the name.
static Bool instance_global(state::Emitter *e, Str name, const ast::Decl **found, Str *key) {
    state::Local local = {};
    if (state::find_local(e, name, &local)) return false;
    Str full = state::msg(format::push(e->instance_scope, name));
    const types::Symbol *target = types::lookup(&e->options.checked->scopes, full);
    if (target == nullptr || target->kind != .variable || target->decl == nullptr || target->decl->from_c ||
        target->decl->kind != .variable)
        return false;
    *found = target->decl;
    *key = full;
    return true;
}

// `autodiff::out`: a global of an imported module (not a header's: `c_constant` took those). The declaration it names
// and its key, `std::autodiff::out`, as the checker keeps it (#1975).
static Bool imported_global(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Expr *x, const ast::Decl **found, Str *key) {
    if (e->options.checked == nullptr) return false;
    if (x->kind == .name && countof(x->kind.name.path.segments) == 1 && countof(e->instance_scope) > 0)
        return instance_global(e, x->kind.name.path.segments[0].text, found, key);
    types::Names names = qualified_names(x);
    const types::Scopes *scopes = &e->options.checked->scopes;
    if (names.count < 2) return false;
    Str prefix = "";
    for (Usize i = 0; i + 1 < names.count; i++) {
        const types::Symbol *module = types::lookup(scopes, state::msg(format::push(prefix, names.items[i])));
        if (module == nullptr || module->kind != .module_name || module->decl->kind != .import_module) return false;
        Str module_path = "";
        for (Usize j = 0; j < countof(module->decl->kind.import_module.path.segments); j++)
            module_path =
                state::msg(format::push(module_path, module->decl->kind.import_module.path.segments[j].text, "::"));
        prefix = module_path;
    }
    Str full = state::msg(format::push(prefix, names.items[names.count - 1]));
    const types::Symbol *target = types::lookup(scopes, full);
    if (target == nullptr || target->kind != .variable || target->decl == nullptr || target->decl->from_c ||
        target->decl->kind != .variable)
        return false;
    *found = target->decl;
    *key = full;
    return true;
}

// Reads an imported module's global: declared external under its `@c_name` (else its key) when first read, then loaded.
static state::Status imported_global_read(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Expr *x, const ast::Decl *d, Str key) {
    types::TypeRef wanted = types::type_of(e->options.checked, x);
    if (wanted == nullptr) return state::fail("the global has no type", x->span);
    state::TyResult made = state::type_of_checked(e, wanted, x->span);
    if (made == .error) return {.error = made.error};
    if (d->kind == .variable && d->kind.variable.is_constexpr && d->kind.variable.init != nullptr &&
        d->kind.variable.init->kind == .integer) { // `pub const op_equal: Op = 0`
        state::push_eval(e, d->kind.variable.init, state::hint_of(made.ok));
        return state::success();
    }
    Str own = state::c_name_of(d);
    char *label = state::cstr(countof(own) > 0 ? own : key);
    c::LLVMValueRef global = c::LLVMGetNamedGlobal(e->module, label);
    if (global == nullptr) global = c::LLVMAddGlobal(e->module, made.ok.llvm, label);
    mem::free(label);
    c::LLVMValueRef loaded = c::LLVMBuildLoad2(e->builder, made.ok.llvm, global, "");
    state::push_value(e, (state::Value){.llvm = loaded, .ty = made.ok});
    return state::success();
}

// `Kind(pair = (a = 1, b = 2))`: a payload enumeration named as the callee with one argument `variant = payload`, which
// the checker typed as `.pair((a = 1, b = 2))` of that enumeration (`enum_variant_call` in front/types_expr.smith). The
// callee is a type, so it has no type of its own. Null when the call is no such form.
static const ast::Expr *named_variant(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Expr *x) {
    if (e->options.checked == nullptr || x->kind != .call || countof(x->kind.call.args) != 1) return nullptr;
    const ast::Expr *arg = x->kind.call.args[0];
    const ast::Expr *callee = x->kind.call.callee;
    if (!(arg->kind == .named_arg)) return nullptr;
    types::TypeRef t = types::type_of(e->options.checked, x);
    if (t == nullptr || !types::is_payload_enum(t)) return nullptr;
    if (types::type_of(e->options.checked, callee) != nullptr) return nullptr; // a function's call
    ast::Expr *variant = mem::alloc(ast::Expr);
    variant->span = x->span;
    variant->kind = {.variant = {.name = arg->kind.named_arg.name, .payload = arg->kind.named_arg.value}};
    return variant;
}

// A call: a vector built by its type, a payload enumeration built by its name, or a call of a function.
static state::Status dispatch_call(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Expr *x, state::Hint hint) {
    if (x->kind != .call) return state::fail("not a call", x->span);
    if (x->kind.call.callee->kind == .call && checked_vector(e, x)) return vectors::construct(e, x);
    const ast::Expr *variant = named_variant(e, x);
    if (variant != nullptr) {
        state::TyResult made = state::type_of_node(e, x); // the enumeration, which the new node has no record of
        if (made == .error) return {.error = made.error};
        return dispatch_variant(e, variant, state::hint_of(made.ok));
    }
    return call::call(e, x, hint);
}

// The expression the checker read in the place of another, emitted in its place.
static state::Status dispatch_twin(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Expr *twin, state::Hint hint) {
    state::push_eval(e, twin, hint);
    return state::success();
}

// Where the walk is, for the driver's crash handler (runtime/front_flag.c, #2984): the declaration whose body is being
// emitted and the kind of the last expression dispatched, in a fixed buffer and a literal, read without allocating.
static char walk_declaration[256];
static const char *walk_kind = "";

// The handler of an expression's kind: it pushes work or one Value. Every kind of front::ast's Expr is named here; the
// ones nobody emits yet are the last line. (A chain of `if`, see `type_of`.)
// The checker's number of the instance being emitted (`types::max_instances` outside one): what it recorded for a
// node of a generic's body is kept per instance.
static Usize instance_index(const state::Emitter *e) {
    Usize index = types::max_instances;
    if (e->options.checked == nullptr) return index;
    for (Usize i = 0; e->instance != nullptr && i < e->options.checked->instance_count; i++) {
        if (&e->options.checked->instances[i] == e->instance) index = i;
    }
    return index;
}

// Whether the checker computed the Bool of this comparison or call (#3039): it has no run-time form.
static Bool is_computed(const state::Emitter *e, const ast::Expr *x, U64 *computed) {
    if ((x->kind != .binary && x->kind != .call) || e->options.checked == nullptr) return false;
    return types::value_in(e->options.checked, x, instance_index(e), computed);
}

static state::Status dispatch_expr(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Expr *x, state::Hint hint) {
    walk_kind = state::expr_kind_name(x).data;
    try debug::expr_location(e, x);
    if (hint.present && (hint.ty.kind == .slice || hint.ty.kind == .block) && is_array_place(e, x))
        return emit_memory::array_as_slice(e, x, hint);
    U64 computed = 0;
    if (is_computed(e, x, &computed)) return control::computed_boolean(e, computed);
    if (x->kind == .integer) return arith::integer_literal(e, x, hint);
    if (x->kind == .character) return character_literal(e, x);
    const ast::Decl *imported = nullptr;
    Str imported_key = "";
    if (imported_global(e, x, &imported, &imported_key)) return imported_global_read(e, x, imported, imported_key);
    const ast::Expr *constant = c_constant(e, x);
    if (constant != nullptr) {
        types::TypeRef wanted = types::type_of(e->options.checked, x);
        state::Hint given = hint;
        if (wanted != nullptr) {
            state::TyResult made = state::type_of_checked(e, wanted, x->span);
            if (made == .error) return {.error = made.error};
            given = state::hint_of(made.ok);
        }
        state::push_eval(e, constant, given);
        return state::success();
    }
    if (x->kind == .name) {
        if (emit_memory::is_global_name(e, x)) return emit_memory::name_ref(e, x);
        return arith::name_ref(e, x, hint);
    }
    if (x->kind == .unary) return dispatch_unary(e, x, x->kind.unary.op, hint);
    if (x->kind == .binary) return dispatch_binary(e, x, x->kind.binary.op, hint);
    if (x->kind == .assign) return arith::assign_op(e, x, hint);
    if (x->kind == .boolean) return control::boolean(e, x, hint);
    if (x->kind == .conditional) return control::conditional(e, x, hint);
    if (x->kind == .call) return dispatch_call(e, x, hint);
    if (x->kind == .array_lit) {
        if (hint.present && hint.ty.kind == .vector) return vectors::list(e, x, hint);
        return emit_memory::array_literal(e, x, hint);
    }
    if (x->kind == .null_pointer) return emit_memory::null_pointer(e, x, hint);
    if (x->kind == .index) return emit_memory::index(e, x, hint);
    if (x->kind == .member) {
        if (is_tuple_member(e, x)) return tupled::member(e, x, hint);
        state::Status function = state::success();
        if (call::module_function_value(e, x, &function)) return function; // `parse_expr.expression` as a value
        return emit_memory::member(e, x, hint);
    }
    if (x->kind == .variant) return dispatch_variant(e, x, hint);
    if (x->kind == .tuple_lit) return tupled::literal(e, x, hint);
    if (x->kind == .lambda) return lambdas::lambda(e, x, hint);
    if (x->kind == .pattern_test) return state::fail("not yet supported: a pattern in an expression", x->span); // #2650
    if (x->kind == .stmt_expr) return dispatch_stmt_expr(e, x, hint);
    if (x->kind == .floating) return arith::float_literal(e, x, hint);
    if (x->kind == .cast) {
        const ast::Expr *operand = x->kind.cast.operand;
        if (checked_floating(e, x) || checked_floating(e, operand)) return arith::float_cast(e, x, hint);
        return emit_memory::cast_expr(e, x, hint);
    }
    if (x->kind == .try_expr) return optional::try_expr(e, x);
    if (x->kind == .query) return emit_memory::query(e, x, hint);
    if (x->kind == .compound) return emit_memory::compound(e, x, hint);
    if (x->kind == .string) return emit_memory::string_literal(e, x, hint);
    if (x->kind == .slice_of) return emit_memory::slice_of(e, x, hint);
    if (x->kind == .type_value && e->options.checked != nullptr) {
        const ast::Expr *made = types::method_of(e->options.checked, x); // `Point(a, b)`: a construction (#1813)
        if (made != nullptr && made->kind == .call) return call::call(e, made, hint);
        if (made != nullptr) return dispatch_twin(e, made, hint); // `High`, `c.EOF`: the name the checker read (#2984)
    }
    // The kind is named outside backticks, so the count's table keeps the kinds apart (#2984).
    return state::failf(x->span, "not emitted yet: this kind of expression (", state::expr_kind_name(x), ")");
}

// The handler that pushes the address of an lvalue.
static state::Status dispatch_place(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Expr *x) {
    if (x->kind == .name) {
        if (emit_memory::is_global_name(e, x)) return emit_memory::place_name(e, x);
        return arith::place_name(e, x);
    }
    if (x->kind == .unary && x->kind.unary.op == .dereference) return emit_memory::place_dereference(e, x);
    if (x->kind == .index) return emit_memory::place_index(e, x);
    if (x->kind == .member) {
        if (is_tuple_member(e, x)) return tupled::place_member(e, x);
        return emit_memory::place_member(e, x);
    }
    return state::fail("this expression is not assignable", x->span);
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Statements B1 emits

static state::Status drop_value(state::Emitter *e, const state::ThenNone *_) {
    _ = state::pop_value(e);
    return state::success();
}

static state::Status expression_statement(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Stmt *s) {
    if (s->kind != .expression) {
        return state::fail("not an expression statement", s->span);
    }
    state::push_then_none(e, (state::ThenNone){.run = drop_value, .span = s->span});
    state::push_eval(e, s->kind.expression.value, state::no_hint());
    return state::success();
}

static state::Status block_close(state::Emitter *e, const state::ThenNone *_) {
    state::end_scope(e);
    return state::success();
}

// The block's end: the scope closes after whatever work `end_of_block` pushed (a deferred statement sees the locals).
static state::Status block_finish(state::Emitter *e, const state::ThenNone *w) {
    state::push_then_none(e, (state::ThenNone){.run = block_close, .span = w->span});
    try control::end_of_block(e, w->span);
    return state::success();
}

static state::Status block_statement(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Stmt *s) {
    if (s->kind != .block) {
        return state::fail("not a block", s->span);
    }
    state::begin_scope(e);
    state::push_then_none(e, (state::ThenNone){.run = block_finish, .span = s->span});
    for (Usize i = countof(s->kind.block.items); i > 0; i--)
        state::push_statement(e, s->kind.block.items[i - 1]);
    return state::success();
}

// The value of the initializer is on the stack: the slot is made, the value stored, the name visible from here on.
static state::Status declare_finish(state::Emitter *e, const state::ThenGeneral *w) {
    const ast::Decl *d = w->decl;
    if (d->kind != .variable) {
        return state::fail("not a variable", w->span);
    }
    Str name = d->kind.variable.name;
    state::Value value = state::pop_value(e);
    state::Ty ty = value.ty;
    if (!w->flag) ty = w->ty;
    if (!state::same_type(ty, value.ty)) {
        try state::convert(e, value, ty, w->span, .initialize);
        value = state::pop_value(e);
    }
    c::LLVMValueRef slot = state::new_alloca(e, ty, name);
    state::apply_align(d, slot);
    state::store(e, value.llvm, slot);
    state::add_local(e, (state::Local){.name = name, .ty = ty, .address = slot});
    try debug::declare_local(e, name, ty, slot, w->span);
    return state::success();
}

// `let mut x: T = undefined`: the slot, and no store, except that with `Options.fill_undefined` (a debug build) the
// slot is filled with the byte 0xAA so that a read before a write shows. There is no zero value (#1428).
static state::Status declare_undefined(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Decl *d, ast::Span span) {
    if (d->kind != .variable) {
        return state::fail("not a variable", span);
    }
    const ast::TypeExpr *type = d->kind.variable.type;
    if (type->kind == .auto_type) return state::fail("`undefined` has no type to take: write the type", span);
    state::TyResult made = type_of(e, type);
    if (made == .error) {
        return {.error = made.error};
    }
    state::Ty ty = made.ok;
    Str name = d->kind.variable.name;
    c::LLVMValueRef slot = state::new_alloca(e, ty, name);
    state::apply_align(d, slot);
    if (e->options.fill_undefined) {
        c::LLVMTypeRef byte = c::LLVMInt8TypeInContext(e->context);
        c::LLVMBuildMemSet(e->builder, slot, c::LLVMConstInt(byte, 0xAA, 0), c::LLVMSizeOf(ty.llvm), 1);
    }
    state::add_local(e, (state::Local){.name = name, .ty = ty, .address = slot});
    try debug::declare_local(e, name, ty, slot, span);
    return state::success();
}

// `x = undefined`: the word, unless a local of that name hides it.
static Bool is_undefined(const ast::Expr *init) {
    if (init == nullptr || !(init->kind == .name)) return false;
    ast::Path path = init->kind.name.path;
    return countof(path.segments) == 1 && state::same_text(path.segments[0].text, "undefined");
}

// Whether a written type is `type` itself: the type of a constant that holds a type.
static Bool names_type_type(const ast::TypeExpr *t) {
    if (t->kind != .named || countof(t->kind.named.path.segments) != 1) return false;
    return state::same_text(t->kind.named.path.segments[0].text, "type");
}

static state::Status local_variable(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Decl *d, ast::Span span) {
    if (d->kind != .variable) {
        return state::fail("not a variable", span);
    }
    const ast::TypeExpr *type = d->kind.variable.type;
    Str name = d->kind.variable.name;
    if (state::same_text(d->kind.variable.name, "_") && d->kind.variable.init != nullptr) {
        // `let _ = f()`: the value is computed and dropped; no slot, no local.
        state::Hint dropped = state::no_hint();
        if (type->kind != .auto_type) {
            state::TyResult made = type_of(e, type);
            if (made == .error) {
                return {.error = made.error};
            }
            dropped = state::hint_of(made.ok);
        }
        state::push_then_none(e, (state::ThenNone){.run = drop_value, .span = span});
        state::push_eval(e, d->kind.variable.init, dropped);
        return state::success();
    }
    // A local `const X = v` is a constant local; today's `constexpr T x` is not emitted yet.
    Bool is_const_local = d->kind.variable.is_constexpr && d->kind.variable.is_new;
    if (d->is_static && !d->is_extern && !d->kind.variable.is_thread_local && d->kind.variable.init != nullptr) {
        state::Ty held = {};
        c::LLVMValueRef global = nullptr; // `static mut buffer: [1024]char = ...`: a private global, same name
        try emit_memory::static_local(e, d, &held, &global);
        state::add_local(e, (state::Local){.name = name, .ty = held, .address = global});
        return state::success();
    }
    if ((d->kind.variable.is_constexpr && !is_const_local) || d->kind.variable.is_thread_local || d->is_static ||
        d->is_extern)
        return state::not_emitted("this kind of variable", span);
    for (Usize i = e->scope_marks[e->scope_count - 1]; i < e->local_count; i++) {
        if (state::same_text(e->locals[i].name, d->kind.variable.name))
            return state::failf(span, d->kind.variable.name, " is declared twice in one scope");
    }
    Bool is_auto = type->kind == .auto_type;
    if (d->kind.variable.init == nullptr)
        return state::failf(span, "`", d->kind.variable.name, "` needs a value: give one, or write `= undefined`");
    state::Local shadow = {};
    if (is_undefined(d->kind.variable.init) && !state::find_local(e, "undefined", &shadow))
        return declare_undefined(e, d, span);
    state::Ty ty = {};
    state::Hint hint = state::no_hint();
    if (!is_auto) {
        state::TyResult made = type_of(e, type);
        if (made == .error) {
            return {.error = made.error};
        }
        ty = made.ok;
        hint = state::hint_of(ty);
    }
    state::push_then_general(
        e, (state::ThenGeneral){.run = declare_finish, .decl = d, .ty = ty, .flag = is_auto, .span = span});
    state::push_eval(e, d->kind.variable.init, hint);
    return state::success();
}

// Whether a local declaration is a constant that holds a type: `const T = typeof(x)`, or one written `: type`.
static Bool holds_type(const state::Emitter *e, const ast::Decl *d) {
    if (d->kind != .variable || e->options.checked == nullptr) return false;
    const ast::TypeExpr *type = d->kind.variable.type;
    const ast::Expr *init = d->kind.variable.init;
    if (!state::is_local_type(d) || (type->kind != .auto_type && !names_type_type(type))) return false;
    U64 marked = 0; // the checker marks the value of one it made a name of a type
    return types::value_in(e->options.checked, init, instance_index(e), &marked);
}

static state::Status declaration_statement(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Stmt *s) {
    if (s->kind != .declaration) {
        return state::fail("not a declaration", s->span);
    }
    const ast::Decl *d = s->kind.declaration.decl;
    if (holds_type(e, d)) {
        // a constant that holds a type: a name of the type from here on, with nothing stored (#3039)
        if (e->local_type_count == countof(e->local_types))
            return state::fail("more than 16 constants that hold a type in one function", s->span);
        e->local_types[e->local_type_count] = d;
        e->local_type_count += 1;
        return state::success();
    }
    if (d->kind == .variable) return local_variable(e, d, s->span);
    if (d->kind == .record) return emit_memory::record_decl(e, d);
    return state::not_emitted("this kind of declaration in a block", s->span);
}

static state::Status ret_value(state::Emitter *e, const state::ThenGeneral *w) {
    c::LLVMBuildRet(e->builder, w->value);
    return state::success();
}

static state::Status ret_void(state::Emitter *e, const state::ThenNone *_) {
    c::LLVMBuildRetVoid(e->builder);
    return state::success();
}

static state::Status return_finish(state::Emitter *e, const state::ThenNone *w) {
    state::Value value = state::pop_value(e);
    if (state::same_type(e->result, void_type(e)) && state::same_type(value.ty, e->result)) {
        // `return f()` where `f` has no result: nothing to return but the end of the function.
        try control::before_return(e, w->span);
        c::LLVMBuildRetVoid(e->builder);
        return state::success();
    }
    if (!state::same_type(value.ty, e->result)) {
        try state::convert(e, value, e->result, w->span, .return_value);
        value = state::pop_value(e);
    }
    // With no `defer` to run after the call, the call is the last thing the function does: a guaranteed tail call.
    if (e->defer_count == 0) call::mark_tail_call(e, value.llvm);
    state::push_then_general(
        e, (state::ThenGeneral){.run = ret_value, .value = value.llvm, .ty = value.ty, .span = w->span});
    try control::before_return(e, w->span);
    return state::success();
}

static state::Status return_statement(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Stmt *s) {
    if (s->kind != .return_stmt) {
        return state::fail("not a return", s->span);
    }
    if (streams::in_body(e)) return streams::return_statement(e, s);
    if (s->kind.return_stmt.value == nullptr) return call::return_void(e, s);
    state::push_then_none(e, (state::ThenNone){.run = return_finish, .span = s->span});
    state::push_eval(e, s->kind.return_stmt.value, state::hint_of(e->result));
    return state::success();
}

// `static_assert(c, "m")`: the checker computed the condition and reported a false or unknown one (#3039), so nothing
// is emitted for it.
static state::Status static_assert_statement(const ast::Stmt *s) {
    if (s->kind != .static_assert_stmt) return state::fail("not a static_assert", s->span);
    return state::success();
}

// A statement after `return` goes into a block nothing jumps to: instructions after a terminator are not valid.
static void start_block_if_ended(state::Emitter *e) {
    c::LLVMBasicBlockRef here = c::LLVMGetInsertBlock(e->builder);
    if (c::LLVMGetBasicBlockTerminator(here) == nullptr) return;
    c::LLVMBasicBlockRef dead = c::LLVMAppendBasicBlockInContext(e->context, e->function, "dead");
    c::LLVMPositionBuilderAtEnd(e->builder, dead);
}

// Whether the checker answered the condition of the `if` `s` in the body being emitted (`is_slice(typeof(a))`, #1902),
// and which branch it kept; the other branch was never checked, so it is not emitted (#2981).
static Bool decided_if(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Stmt *s, const ast::Stmt **live) {
    if (s->kind == .if_stmt && e->options.checked != nullptr) {
        Usize index = instance_index(e);
        Bool keeps_then = false;
        if (types::decided_in(e->options.checked, s->kind.if_stmt.condition, index, &keeps_then)) {
            *live = keeps_then ? s->kind.if_stmt.then_branch : s->kind.if_stmt.else_branch;
            return true;
        }
    }
    return false;
}

static state::Status dispatch_statement(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Stmt *s) {
    start_block_if_ended(e);
    try debug::stmt_location(e, s);
    const ast::Stmt *live = nullptr;
    if (decided_if(e, s, &live)) {
        if (live != nullptr) state::push_statement(e, live);
        return state::success();
    }
    if (s->kind == .expression) return expression_statement(e, s);
    if (s->kind == .declaration) return declaration_statement(e, s);
    if (s->kind == .block) return block_statement(e, s);
    if (s->kind == .return_stmt) return return_statement(e, s);
    if (s->kind == .if_stmt) return control::if_stmt(e, s);
    if (s->kind == .while_stmt) return control::while_stmt(e, s);
    if (s->kind == .do_while) return control::do_while(e, s);
    if (s->kind == .for_stmt) return control::for_stmt(e, s);
    if (s->kind == .switch_stmt) return control::switch_stmt(e, s);
    if (s->kind == .break_stmt) return control::break_stmt(e, s);
    if (s->kind == .continue_stmt) return control::continue_stmt(e, s);
    if (s->kind == .defer_stmt) return control::defer_stmt(e, s);
    if (s->kind == .errdefer_stmt) return control::errdefer_stmt(e, s);
    if (s->kind == .goto_stmt) return control::goto_stmt(e, s);
    if (s->kind == .labeled) return control::labeled(e, s);
    if (s->kind == .empty) return state::success();
    if (s->kind == .match_stmt) return matching::match_stmt(e, s);
    if (s->kind == .for_in) return looping::for_in(e, s);
    if (s->kind == .if_let) return matching::if_let(e, s);
    if (s->kind == .destructure) return tupled::destructure(e, s);
    if (s->kind == .yield_stmt) return streams::yield_statement(e, s);
    if (s->kind == .static_assert_stmt) return static_assert_statement(s);
    return state::not_emitted("this kind of statement", s->span);
}

// Call a `then` item's continuation with its data, at the location of the node that pushed it.
static state::Status run_then(state::Emitter *e, state::Then then) {
    switch (then) {
    case .none:
        try debug::then_location(e, then.none.span);
        return then.none.run(e, &then.none);
    case .expr:
        try debug::then_location(e, then.expr.span);
        return then.expr.run(e, &then.expr);
    case .blocks:
        try debug::then_location(e, then.blocks.span);
        return then.blocks.run(e, &then.blocks);
    case .general:
        try debug::then_location(e, then.general.span);
        return then.general.run(e, &then.general);
    }
}

// Run the work stack until it is empty or a handler fails.
static state::Status run(state::Emitter *e) {
    while (e->work_count > 0) {
        e->work_count -= 1;
        state::Work item = e->work[e->work_count];
        switch (item) {
        case .eval:
            try dispatch_expr(e, item.eval.expr, item.eval.hint);
            break;
        case .place:
            try dispatch_place(e, item.place.expr);
            break;
        case .statement:
            try dispatch_statement(e, item.statement.stmt);
            break;
        case .then:
            try run_then(e, item.then);
            break;
        }
    }
    return state::success();
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Functions

// `front::test` and `add` as `front::test::add`.
static Str symbol_of(const ast::Module *m, Str name) {
    Str symbol = state::msg(format::push(name));
    for (Usize i = countof(m->name.segments); i > 0; i--) {
        Str longer = state::msg(format::push(m->name.segments[i - 1].text, "::", symbol));
        state::free_text(symbol);
        symbol = longer;
    }
    return symbol;
}

static Bool is_string(const ast::Expr *x) {
    return x->kind == .string;
}

// The LLVM name: the c_name if there is one, `main` for a `main`, else the module path joined with `::`. A fresh
// string the caller frees.
static Str function_symbol(const ast::Module *m, const ast::Decl *d, Str name) {
    Str own = state::c_name_of(d);
    if (countof(own) > 0) return state::msg(format::push(own));
    if (state::same_text(name, "main")) return state::msg(format::push(name));
    return symbol_of(m, name);
}

static state::Status check_function(const ast::Decl *d) {
    if (d->kind != .function) {
        return state::fail("not a function", d->span);
    }
    ast::Param params[:] = d->kind.function.params;
    for (Usize i = 0; i < countof(d->attributes); i++) {
        if (!state::is_c_name(d->attributes[i])) continue;
        ast::Attribute attribute = d->attributes[i];
        if (countof(attribute.args) != 1 || !is_string(attribute.args[0]))
            return state::fail("`@c_name` takes one string", attribute.span);
    }
    for (Usize i = 0; i < countof(params); i++) {
        if (params[i].is_constexpr || params[i].is_rest)
            return state::not_emitted("constexpr or rest parameter", params[i].span);
    }
    return state::success();
}

static void add_function(state::Emitter *e, state::FunctionInfo info) {
    if (e->function_count == countof(e->functions)) {
        Usize capacity = countof(e->functions) * 2;
        if (capacity < 16) capacity = 16;
        e->functions = mem::realloc(e->functions, capacity);
    }
    e->functions[e->function_count] = info;
    e->function_count += 1;
}

// `[[std::inline]]`, `[[std::noinline]]` and `[[std::cold]]` are the LLVM function attributes `alwaysinline`,
// `noinline` and `cold` (the function index of an attribute list is all ones).
static void add_function_attributes(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Decl *d, c::LLVMValueRef function) {
    for (Usize i = 0; i < countof(d->attributes); i++) {
        ast::Path name = d->attributes[i].name;
        Usize n = countof(name.segments);
        if (n == 0 || n > 2 || (n == 2 && !state::same_text(name.segments[0].text, "std"))) continue;
        Str word = name.segments[n - 1].text;
        Str kind = "";
        if (state::same_text(word, "inline")) kind = "alwaysinline";
        if (state::same_text(word, "noinline")) kind = "noinline";
        if (state::same_text(word, "cold")) kind = "cold";
        if (countof(kind) == 0) continue;
        U32 id = c::LLVMGetEnumAttributeKindForName(kind.data, countof(kind));
        c::LLVMAddAttributeAtIndex(function, 0xFFFFFFFF, c::LLVMCreateEnumAttribute(e->context, id, 0));
    }
}

static Bool is_slice(state::Ty ty) {
    return ty.kind == .slice;
}

// The end of a C `main` around smith's: the body's result, or 0 for a `main` with none (C's own `main` returns 0 at
// its end; without it the exit status was whatever the last call left in the register, #2853).
static void finish_entry(state::Emitter *e, c::LLVMBuilderRef b, c::LLVMTypeRef body_type, c::LLVMValueRef called) {
    c::LLVMTypeRef result = c::LLVMGetReturnType(body_type);
    if (c::LLVMGetTypeKind(result) == c::LLVMVoidTypeKind)
        c::LLVMBuildRet(b, c::LLVMConstInt(c::LLVMInt32TypeInContext(e->context), 0, 0));
    else
        c::LLVMBuildRet(b, called);
    c::LLVMDisposeBuilder(b);
}

// `main(args: []str)` is C's `int main(int argc, char **argv)`: it builds argc slices on the stack, each pointing into
// argv's own characters (not copied), and calls the body, which was declared as the internal `main.args`.
static void add_args_entry(state::Emitter *e, c::LLVMValueRef body, c::LLVMTypeRef body_type, c::LLVMTypeRef args,
                           c::LLVMTypeRef cell_type) {
    c::LLVMTypeRef word = c::LLVMInt64TypeInContext(e->context);
    if (e->target_data != nullptr) word = c::LLVMIntPtrTypeInContext(e->context, e->target_data);
    c::LLVMTypeRef pointer = c::LLVMPointerTypeInContext(e->context, 0);
    c::LLVMTypeRef int32 = c::LLVMInt32TypeInContext(e->context);
    c::LLVMTypeRef main_params[2] = {int32, pointer};
    c::LLVMTypeRef main_type = c::LLVMFunctionType(int32, main_params, 2, 0);
    c::LLVMValueRef main_function = c::LLVMAddFunction(e->module, "main", main_type);
    c::LLVMSetLinkage(main_function, c::LLVMExternalLinkage);
    c::LLVMTypeRef length_params[1] = {pointer};
    c::LLVMTypeRef length_type = c::LLVMFunctionType(word, length_params, 1, 0);
    c::LLVMValueRef length = c::LLVMGetNamedFunction(e->module, "strlen");
    if (length == nullptr) length = c::LLVMAddFunction(e->module, "strlen", length_type);
    c::LLVMBuilderRef b = c::LLVMCreateBuilderInContext(e->context);
    c::LLVMBasicBlockRef entry = c::LLVMAppendBasicBlockInContext(e->context, main_function, "entry");
    c::LLVMBasicBlockRef test = c::LLVMAppendBasicBlockInContext(e->context, main_function, "test");
    c::LLVMBasicBlockRef step = c::LLVMAppendBasicBlockInContext(e->context, main_function, "step");
    c::LLVMBasicBlockRef done = c::LLVMAppendBasicBlockInContext(e->context, main_function, "done");
    c::LLVMValueRef argc = c::LLVMGetParam(main_function, 0);
    c::LLVMValueRef argv = c::LLVMGetParam(main_function, 1);
    c::LLVMPositionBuilderAtEnd(b, entry);
    c::LLVMValueRef count = c::LLVMBuildSExt(b, argc, word, "count");
    c::LLVMValueRef cells = c::LLVMBuildArrayAlloca(b, cell_type, count, "cells");
    c::LLVMValueRef index = c::LLVMBuildAlloca(b, word, "index");
    c::LLVMBuildStore(b, c::LLVMConstInt(word, 0, 0), index);
    c::LLVMBuildBr(b, test);
    c::LLVMPositionBuilderAtEnd(b, test);
    c::LLVMValueRef at = c::LLVMBuildLoad2(b, word, index, "at");
    c::LLVMBuildCondBr(b, c::LLVMBuildICmp(b, c::LLVMIntULT, at, count, "more"), step, done);
    c::LLVMPositionBuilderAtEnd(b, step);
    c::LLVMValueRef from[1] = {at};
    c::LLVMValueRef slot = c::LLVMBuildGEP2(b, pointer, argv, from, 1, "slot");
    c::LLVMValueRef text = c::LLVMBuildLoad2(b, pointer, slot, "text");
    c::LLVMValueRef size = c::LLVMBuildCall2(b, length_type, length, &text, 1, "size");
    c::LLVMValueRef cell = c::LLVMBuildGEP2(b, cell_type, cells, from, 1, "cell");
    c::LLVMBuildStore(b, text, c::LLVMBuildStructGEP2(b, cell_type, cell, 0, "data"));
    c::LLVMBuildStore(b, size, c::LLVMBuildStructGEP2(b, cell_type, cell, 1, "count"));
    c::LLVMBuildStore(b, c::LLVMBuildAdd(b, at, c::LLVMConstInt(word, 1, 0), "next"), index);
    c::LLVMBuildBr(b, test);
    c::LLVMPositionBuilderAtEnd(b, done);
    c::LLVMValueRef slice = c::LLVMGetUndef(args);
    slice = c::LLVMBuildInsertValue(b, slice, cells, 0, "data");
    slice = c::LLVMBuildInsertValue(b, slice, count, 1, "count");
    finish_entry(e, b, body_type, c::LLVMBuildCall2(b, body_type, body, &slice, 1, ""));
}

// `fn main():` with no result is C's `int main(void)` returning 0 around the body, declared as the internal
// `main.body`.
static void add_plain_entry(state::Emitter *e, c::LLVMValueRef body, c::LLVMTypeRef body_type) {
    c::LLVMTypeRef int32 = c::LLVMInt32TypeInContext(e->context);
    c::LLVMValueRef main_function = c::LLVMAddFunction(e->module, "main", c::LLVMFunctionType(int32, nullptr, 0, 0));
    c::LLVMSetLinkage(main_function, c::LLVMExternalLinkage);
    c::LLVMBuilderRef b = c::LLVMCreateBuilderInContext(e->context);
    c::LLVMPositionBuilderAtEnd(b, c::LLVMAppendBasicBlockInContext(e->context, main_function, "entry"));
    finish_entry(e, b, body_type, c::LLVMBuildCall2(b, body_type, body, nullptr, 0, ""));
}

// Pass 2: the function's symbol, type and linkage.
static state::Status declare_function(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Decl *d) {
    if (d->kind != .function) {
        return state::fail("not a function", d->span);
    }
    Str name = d->kind.function.name;
    ast::Param source_params[:] = d->kind.function.params;
    const ast::TypeExpr *result_type = d->kind.function.result;
    try check_function(d);
    for (Usize i = 0; i < e->function_count; i++) {
        if (state::same_text(e->functions[i].name, name)) return state::failf(d->span, name, " is declared twice");
    }
    Usize count = countof(source_params);
    state::Ty params[:] = mem::alloc_slice(state::Ty, count + 1);
    if (count > 64) return state::not_emitted("more than 64 parameters", d->span);
    c::LLVMTypeRef parameter_types[64];
    for (Usize i = 0; i < count; i++) {
        state::TyResult made = type_of(e, source_params[i].type);
        if (made == .error) {
            return {.error = made.error};
        }
        params[i] = made.ok;
        parameter_types[i] = state::abi_type(e, params[i]);
    }
    state::Ty result = void_type(e);
    if (result_type != nullptr) {
        state::TyResult made_result = type_of(e, result_type);
        if (made_result == .error) {
            return {.error = made_result.error};
        }
        result = made_result.ok;
    }
    I32 variadic = 0; // a body that reads `...` with va_start
    if (d->kind == .function && d->kind.function.variadic) variadic = 1;
    c::LLVMTypeRef type = c::LLVMFunctionType(result.llvm, parameter_types, (U32)count, variadic);
    Bool takes_args = state::same_text(name, "main") && count == 1 && is_slice(params[0]);
    Bool plain_main =
        state::same_text(name, "main") && count == 0 && c::LLVMGetTypeKind(result.llvm) == c::LLVMVoidTypeKind;
    Str symbol = function_symbol(e->tree, d, name);
    if (takes_args) symbol = state::msg(format::push("main.args"));
    if (plain_main) symbol = state::msg(format::push("main.body"));
    char *label = state::cstr(symbol);
    c::LLVMValueRef function = c::LLVMAddFunction(e->module, label, type);
    mem::free(label);
    add_function_attributes(e, d, function);
    Bool external = d->exported || d->is_pub || countof(state::c_name_of(d)) > 0 || state::same_text(name, "main");
    if (takes_args || plain_main) external = false;
    // A private function of a module is external but hidden (#2853): a generic instance of the module that another
    // object emits (`console.print` in the program's object) calls it from there. Its symbol is the module's
    // (`std::console::emit_long`), so no other object has it; `static`, and the wrapper of a `main` with arguments,
    // stay internal.
    Bool hidden = !external && !takes_args && !plain_main && !d->is_static;
    if (external || hidden)
        c::LLVMSetLinkage(function, c::LLVMExternalLinkage);
    else
        c::LLVMSetLinkage(function, c::LLVMInternalLinkage);
    if (hidden) c::LLVMSetVisibility(function, c::LLVMHiddenVisibility);
    add_function(e, (state::FunctionInfo){.name = name,
                                          .symbol = symbol,
                                          .llvm = function,
                                          .llvm_type = type,
                                          .result = result,
                                          .variadic = variadic != 0,
                                          .params = params[0:count]});
    if (takes_args) {
        state::Ty args = params[0];
        if (args.kind == .slice) add_args_entry(e, function, type, args.llvm, args.kind.slice.element->llvm);
    }
    if (plain_main) add_plain_entry(e, function, type);

    return state::success();
}

// Whether `d` is a generic function: a template emits nothing, its instances are emitted (#1909).
static Bool is_template(const ast::Decl *d) {
    if (d->kind != .function) return false;
    if (countof(d->kind.function.generics) > 0) return true;
    ast::Param params[:] = d->kind.function.params;
    for (Usize i = 0; i < countof(params); i++) {
        if (types::is_compile_time(&params[i]) || types::is_auto_param(&params[i])) return true;
    }
    return false;
}

// Pass 2 for an instance the checker made: its symbol is `module::alloc.i32`, its types are the checker's.
static state::Status declare_instance(state::Emitter *e, const types::Instance *instance) {
    const ast::Decl *d = instance->decl;
    if (d->kind != .function) {
        return state::fail("not a function", d->span);
    }
    Str name = state::instance_name(instance);
    types::TypeRef signature = instance->signature;
    Usize count = countof(types::slots_of(signature).items);
    if (count > 64) return state::not_emitted("more than 64 parameters", d->span);
    state::Ty params[:] = mem::alloc_slice(state::Ty, count + 1);
    c::LLVMTypeRef llvm_types[64];
    for (Usize i = 0; i < count; i++) {
        state::TyResult made = type_of_checked(e, types::slots_of(signature).items[i].type, d->span);
        if (made == .error) {
            return {.error = made.error};
        }
        params[i] = made.ok;
        llvm_types[i] = state::abi_type(e, params[i]);
    }
    state::Ty result = void_type(e);
    if (types::element_of(signature) != nullptr &&
        types::element_of(signature) != e->options.checked->table.void_type) {
        state::TyResult made_result = type_of_checked(e, types::element_of(signature), d->span);
        if (made_result == .error) {
            return {.error = made_result.error};
        }
        result = made_result.ok;
    }
    I32 variadic = 0;
    if (d->kind == .function && d->kind.function.variadic) variadic = 1;
    c::LLVMTypeRef type = c::LLVMFunctionType(result.llvm, llvm_types, (U32)count, variadic);
    Str symbol = function_symbol(e->tree, d, name);
    char *label = state::cstr(symbol);
    c::LLVMValueRef function = c::LLVMAddFunction(e->module, label, type);
    mem::free(label);
    c::LLVMSetLinkage(function, c::LLVMInternalLinkage);
    add_function(e, (state::FunctionInfo){.name = name,
                                          .symbol = symbol,
                                          .llvm = function,
                                          .llvm_type = type,
                                          .result = result,
                                          .variadic = variadic != 0,
                                          .params = params[0:count]});
    return state::success();
}

// The function's entry block: the slots come first and a branch leads to the body, which is where code goes.
static void start_function(state::Emitter *e, state::FunctionInfo info) {
    e->function = info.llvm;
    e->result = info.result;
    e->trap_block = nullptr;
    e->local_count = 0;
    e->scope_count = 0;
    e->local_type_count = 0;
    e->work_count = 0;
    e->value_count = 0;
    c::LLVMBasicBlockRef entry = c::LLVMAppendBasicBlockInContext(e->context, info.llvm, "entry");
    c::LLVMBasicBlockRef body = c::LLVMAppendBasicBlockInContext(e->context, info.llvm, "body");
    c::LLVMPositionBuilderAtEnd(e->builder, entry);
    // The previous function's location must not reach this function's branch (its subprogram is another one, #1979).
    c::LLVMSetCurrentDebugLocation2(e->builder, nullptr);
    c::LLVMSetCurrentDebugLocation2(e->alloca_builder, nullptr);
    c::LLVMValueRef jump = c::LLVMBuildBr(e->builder, body);
    c::LLVMPositionBuilderBefore(e->alloca_builder, jump);
    c::LLVMPositionBuilderAtEnd(e->builder, body);
    e->entry_block = entry;
}

// Parameters live in slots like locals: loaded and stored, the optimizer's mem2reg is not ours.
static state::Status declare_params(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Decl *d, state::FunctionInfo info) {
    if (d->kind != .function) {
        return state::fail("not a function", d->span);
    }
    ast::Param params[:] = d->kind.function.params;
    for (Usize i = 0; i < countof(params); i++) {
        ast::Param p = params[i];
        c::LLVMValueRef value = c::LLVMGetParam(info.llvm, (U32)i);
        c::LLVMSetValueName2(value, p.name.data, countof(p.name));
        c::LLVMValueRef slot = state::new_alloca(e, info.params[i], p.name);
        // An array arrives as a pointer to the caller's elements: the parameter is a copy of them, in its own slot.
        state::Ty param = info.params[i];
        if (param.kind == .array) value = c::LLVMBuildLoad2(e->builder, param.llvm, value, "copy");
        c::LLVMBuildStore(e->builder, value, slot);
        state::add_local(e, (state::Local){.name = p.name, .ty = info.params[i], .address = slot});
        try debug::declare_local(e, p.name, info.params[i], slot, p.span);
    }
    return state::success();
}

// The last line of a body is its value: a body block whose last item is an expression statement.
static Bool is_expression_statement(const ast::Stmt *s) {
    return s->kind == .expression;
}

static Bool ends_in_expression(const ast::Stmt *body) {
    if (body->kind == .block) {
        ast::StmtRef items[:] = body->kind.block.items;
        return countof(items) > 0 && is_expression_statement(items[countof(items) - 1]);
    }
    return false;
}

// Whether the body's last line calls a module function declared `[[noreturn]]` (`stop(...)`): it has no value, so the
// body is emitted as statements and the end of the function is never reached (#2510).
static Bool ends_in_noreturn_call(const state::Emitter *e, const ast::Stmt *body) {
    if (body->kind != .block) return false;
    ast::StmtRef items[:] = body->kind.block.items;
    const ast::Stmt *last = countof(items) > 0 ? items[countof(items) - 1] : nullptr;
    if (last == nullptr || !is_expression_statement(last) || last->kind != .expression) return false;
    const ast::Expr *value = last->kind.expression.value;
    if (value->kind != .call || value->kind.call.callee->kind != .name) return false;
    ast::Path path = value->kind.call.callee->kind.name.path;
    if (countof(path.segments) != 1) return false;
    for (Usize i = 0; i < countof(e->tree->decls); i++) {
        const ast::Decl *d = e->tree->decls[i];
        if (d->kind != .function || !state::same_text(d->kind.function.name, path.segments[0].text)) continue;
        for (Usize k = 0; k < countof(d->attributes); k++) {
            ast::Path name = d->attributes[k].name;
            if (countof(name.segments) == 1 && state::same_text(name.segments[0].text, "noreturn")) return true;
        }
    }
    return false;
}

// The last line's value after a line that returned (`return 1` then `2`, or a compile-time `if` that kept a `return`,
// #2277) goes into a block nothing jumps to, as a statement does.
static state::Status value_after_end(state::Emitter *e, const state::ThenGeneral *w) {
    (void)w;
    start_block_if_ended(e);
    return state::success();
}

// The body block with its last expression returned as `return <expression>` is: the same continuation.
static state::Status value_block(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Stmt *body) {
    try debug::stmt_location(e, body);
    if (body->kind != .block) {
        return state::fail("not a block", body->span);
    }
    ast::StmtRef items[:] = body->kind.block.items;
    const ast::Stmt *last = items[countof(items) - 1];
    if (last->kind != .expression) {
        return state::fail("not an expression statement", last->span);
    }
    ast::Expr *value = last->kind.expression.value;
    state::begin_scope(e);
    state::push_then_none(e, (state::ThenNone){.run = block_finish, .span = body->span});
    state::push_then_none(e, (state::ThenNone){.run = return_finish, .span = last->span});
    state::push_eval(e, value, state::hint_of(e->result));
    state::push_then_general(e, (state::ThenGeneral){.run = value_after_end, .span = last->span});
    for (Usize i = countof(items) - 1; i > 0; i--)
        state::push_statement(e, items[i - 1]);
    return state::success();
}

// A block whose last line is an expression or a `match` has a value; one that ends in `return`, a loop or nothing
// does not (an old-syntax `if (c) { return a; } else { return b; }` stays a statement). The branch of a one-line `if b:
// 1 else: 0` is the expression itself (#2984: as a body's last line it fell off the end, an `unreachable`).
static Bool block_gives_value(const ast::Stmt *s) {
    if (s->kind == .expression) return true;
    if (s->kind == .block) {
        ast::StmtRef items[:] = s->kind.block.items;
        if (countof(items) == 0) {
            return false;
        }
        const ast::Stmt *last = items[countof(items) - 1];
        return last->kind == .expression || last->kind == .match_stmt;
    }
    return false;
}

// A last line that is a `match`, a block with a value, or an `if` with an `else` whose branches have one (an `else
// if` counts) is the function's value (`value_of`).
static Bool ends_in_value_statement(const ast::Stmt *body) {
    if (body->kind == .block) {
        ast::StmtRef items[:] = body->kind.block.items;
        if (countof(items) == 0) {
            return false;
        }
        const ast::Stmt *last = items[countof(items) - 1];
        if (last->kind == .match_stmt) {
            return true;
        }
        if (last->kind == .block) {
            return block_gives_value(last);
        }
        if (last->kind == .if_stmt) {
            const ast::Stmt *otherwise = last->kind.if_stmt.else_branch;
            const ast::Stmt *then_branch = last->kind.if_stmt.then_branch;
            if (otherwise == nullptr || !block_gives_value(then_branch)) {
                return false;
            }
            return otherwise->kind == .if_stmt || block_gives_value(otherwise);
        }
    }
    return false;
}

// Runs after the statements before the last line: its handler pushes the one Value `return_finish` takes.
static state::Status value_start(state::Emitter *e, const state::ThenGeneral *w) {
    const ast::Stmt *s = w->stmt;
    if (s->kind == .match_stmt) return matching::value_of(e, s, w->hint);
    return blockval::value_of(e, s, w->hint);
}

// A block whose last line is an expression, with that line written as `return <expression>` (#2709), or null.
static ast::Stmt *returning_block(const ast::Stmt *b) {
    if (b->kind != .block || countof(b->kind.block.items) == 0) return nullptr;
    ast::StmtRef items[:] = b->kind.block.items;
    Usize count = countof(items);
    const ast::Stmt *last = items[count - 1];
    if (last->kind != .expression) return nullptr;
    ast::StmtRef *room = (ast::StmtRef *)mem::alloc_array_raw(sizeof(ast::StmtRef), count, alignof(ast::StmtRef));
    for (Usize i = 0; i + 1 < count; i++)
        room[i] = items[i];
    room[count - 1] = ast::return_value(last->kind.expression.value);
    room[count - 1]->span = last->span;
    ast::StmtRef list[:] = room[0:count];
    ast::Stmt *made = ast::block(list);
    made->span = b->span;
    mem::free((void *)room);
    return made;
}

// An `if` (with `else if` and `else`) whose every branch ends in an expression, with each branch's last line
// written as `return <expression>`, so a call there is in tail position (#2709). Null for anything else: a branch that
// is not such a block, no `else`, or a chain of more than 32. The chain is read with a loop, not recursion.
static ast::Stmt *returning_if(const ast::Stmt *s) {
    const ast::Stmt *chain[32];
    Usize count = 0;
    const ast::Stmt *current = s;
    ast::Stmt *tail = nullptr;
    while (tail == nullptr) {
        if (current->kind != .if_stmt || current->kind.if_stmt.is_constexpr || count == 32) return nullptr;
        const ast::Stmt *otherwise = current->kind.if_stmt.else_branch;
        if (otherwise == nullptr || current->kind.if_stmt.then_branch->kind != .block) return nullptr;
        chain[count++] = current;
        if (otherwise->kind == .if_stmt)
            current = otherwise;
        else if (otherwise->kind == .block) {
            tail = returning_block(otherwise);
            if (tail == nullptr) return nullptr;
        } else
            return nullptr;
    }
    for (Usize i = count; i > 0; i--) {
        const ast::Stmt *node = chain[i - 1];
        if (node->kind != .if_stmt) return nullptr;
        ast::Stmt *then_branch = returning_block(node->kind.if_stmt.then_branch);
        if (then_branch == nullptr) return nullptr;
        ast::Stmt copy = *node;
        if (copy.kind != .if_stmt) return nullptr;
        copy.kind.if_stmt.then_branch = then_branch;
        copy.kind.if_stmt.else_branch = tail;
        tail = ast::new_stmt(copy);
    }
    return tail;
}

// A `match` whose every arm is an expression (or already a `return`), with each arm written as `return <expression>`,
// so a call that ends an arm is in tail position (#2709). Null when an arm is a block or another statement.
static ast::Stmt *returning_match(const ast::Stmt *s) {
    if (s->kind != .match_stmt) return nullptr;
    ast::MatchArm arms[:] = s->kind.match_stmt.arms;
    Usize count = countof(arms);
    if (count == 0 || count > 64) return nullptr;
    for (Usize i = 0; i < count; i++) {
        const ast::Expr *value = arms[i].value;
        if (value->kind == .stmt_expr && value->kind.stmt_expr.stmt->kind != .return_stmt) return nullptr;
    }
    ast::MatchArm *room = (ast::MatchArm *)mem::alloc_array_raw(sizeof(ast::MatchArm), count, alignof(ast::MatchArm));
    for (Usize i = 0; i < count; i++) {
        room[i] = arms[i];
        const ast::Expr *given = arms[i].value;
        if (given->kind != .stmt_expr) {
            ast::Stmt *made = ast::return_value(arms[i].value);
            made->span = arms[i].span;
            room[i].value = ast::stmt_expr(made);
            room[i].value->span = arms[i].value->span;
        }
    }
    ast::MatchArm list[:] = room[0:count];
    ast::Stmt *made = ast::match_stmt(s->kind.match_stmt.value, list);
    made->span = s->span;
    mem::free((void *)room);
    return made;
}

// The body with its last `if`, `match` or block returned: as `value_block`, through the same continuation.
static state::Status value_statement_block(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Stmt *body) {
    try debug::stmt_location(e, body);
    if (body->kind != .block) {
        return state::fail("not a block", body->span);
    }
    ast::StmtRef items[:] = body->kind.block.items;
    const ast::Stmt *last = items[countof(items) - 1];
    ast::Stmt *returning = nullptr;
    if (last->kind == .if_stmt) returning = returning_if(last);
    if (last->kind == .match_stmt) returning = returning_match(last);
    if (returning != nullptr) {
        // Each branch returns its own value, so a call that ends a branch is a tail call (#2709).
        state::begin_scope(e);
        state::push_then_none(e, (state::ThenNone){.run = block_finish, .span = body->span});
        state::push_statement(e, returning);
        state::push_then_general(e, (state::ThenGeneral){.run = value_after_end, .span = last->span});
        for (Usize i = countof(items) - 1; i > 0; i--)
            state::push_statement(e, items[i - 1]);
        return state::success();
    }
    state::begin_scope(e);
    state::push_then_none(e, (state::ThenNone){.run = block_finish, .span = body->span});
    state::push_then_none(e, (state::ThenNone){.run = return_finish, .span = last->span});
    state::push_then_general(
        e,
        (state::ThenGeneral){.run = value_start, .stmt = last, .hint = state::hint_of(e->result), .span = last->span});
    state::push_then_general(e, (state::ThenGeneral){.run = value_after_end, .span = last->span});
    for (Usize i = countof(items) - 1; i > 0; i--)
        state::push_statement(e, items[i - 1]);
    return state::success();
}

// A generator (#1546): the ramp under the function's own symbol, then the body as its own function.
static state::Status emit_generator(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Decl *d, state::FunctionInfo info) {
    if (d->kind != .function) {
        return state::fail("not a function", d->span);
    }
    const ast::Stmt *written = d->kind.function.body;
    start_function(e, info);
    try streams::ramp(e, d, info);
    state::FunctionInfo body = streams::body_info(e, info);
    start_function(e, body);
    state::begin_scope(e);
    try streams::body_prologue(e, d, info);
    state::push_statement(e, written);
    try run(e);
    c::LLVMBasicBlockRef last = c::LLVMGetInsertBlock(e->builder);
    if (c::LLVMGetBasicBlockTerminator(last) == nullptr) {
        try streams::end_body(e, d->span);
        try run(e);
    }
    state::end_scope(e);
    return state::success();
}

// Pass 3: one body.
// The compile-time constants of an instance (`n` of `table(64)`) are locals holding their value.
static state::Status declare_constants(state::Emitter *e, const types::Instance *instance, ast::Span span) {
    for (Usize i = 0; i < countof(instance->bindings); i++) {
        types::Binding binding = instance->bindings[i];
        if (binding.is_type) continue;
        state::TyResult made = type_of_checked(e, binding.type, span);
        if (made == .error) {
            return {.error = made.error};
        }
        state::Ty ty = made.ok;
        c::LLVMValueRef slot = state::new_alloca(e, ty, binding.name);
        c::LLVMBuildStore(e->builder, c::LLVMConstInt(ty.llvm, binding.value, 0), slot);
        state::add_local(e, (state::Local){.name = binding.name, .ty = ty, .address = slot});
    }
    return state::success();
}

static state::Status emit_function(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Decl *d, state::FunctionInfo info,
                                   const types::Instance *instance) {
    if (d->kind != .function) {
        return state::fail("not a function", d->span);
    }
    const ast::Stmt *body = d->kind.function.body;
    e->instance = instance;
    if (streams::is_generator_function(info.result, types_stream::has_yield(body))) return emit_generator(e, d, info);
    start_function(e, info);
    state::begin_scope(e);
    try debug::begin_function(e, d);
    try declare_params(e, d, info);
    if (instance != nullptr) try declare_constants(e, instance, d->span);
    Bool is_void_result = c::LLVMGetTypeKind(info.result.llvm) == c::LLVMVoidTypeKind;
    if (!is_void_result && ends_in_value_statement(body)) {
        try value_statement_block(e, body);
    } else if (is_void_result || !ends_in_expression(body) || ends_in_noreturn_call(e, body)) {
        state::push_statement(e, body);
    } else {
        try value_block(e, body);
    }
    try run(e);
    // The end of a function reached without `return`: a `Void` function returns, any other traps.
    c::LLVMBasicBlockRef last = c::LLVMGetInsertBlock(e->builder);
    if (c::LLVMGetBasicBlockTerminator(last) == nullptr) {
        if (is_void_result) {
            state::push_then_none(e, (state::ThenNone){.run = ret_void, .span = d->span});
            try control::before_return(e, d->span);
            try run(e);
        } else {
            arith::trap_here(e);
        }
    }
    state::end_scope(e);
    return state::success();
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The hooks of emit_state

static state::Ty *own_type(state::Emitter *e, state::Ty element) {
    state::OwnedTy *block = mem::alloc(state::OwnedTy);
    block->ty = element;
    block->next = e->owned;
    e->owned = block;
    return &block->ty;
}

static Bool find_record_by_name(state::Emitter *e, Str name, state::Ty *ty) {
    for (Usize i = 0; i < e->record_count; i++) {
        if (state::same_text(e->records[i].name, name)) {
            *ty = e->records[i].ty;
            return true;
        }
    }
    return false;
}

// Whether a checker name has a module before it, `words::Pair`: a record of another smith module.
static Bool in_module(Str name) {
    for (Usize i = 0; i + 1 < countof(name); i++) {
        if (name[i] == ':' && name[i + 1] == ':') return true;
    }
    return false;
}

// Whether a checker name starts with `c::`: it came from a C header.
static Bool from_header(Str name) {
    return countof(name) > 3 && name[0] == 'c' && name[1] == ':' && name[2] == ':';
}

// An integer or `bool` the checker names, by its bits and signedness when the spelling is not one the emitter knows.
static Bool scalar_of_checked(state::Emitter *e, types::TypeRef t, state::Ty *ty) {
    if (t->kind == .bool_type) return state::scalar_type(e, "bool", ty);
    if (t->kind == .floating) {
        Str spelled = "F64";
        if (types::bits_of(t) == 16) spelled = types::name_of(t);
        if (types::bits_of(t) == 32) spelled = "F32";
        return arith::type_float(e, spelled, ty);
    }
    if (t->kind != .integer) return false;
    if (state::scalar_type(e, types::name_of(t), ty)) return true;
    Bool is_signed = types::signed_of(t);
    if (types::bits_of(t) == 8) return state::scalar_type(e, is_signed ? "i8" : "u8", ty);
    if (types::bits_of(t) == 16) return state::scalar_type(e, is_signed ? "i16" : "u16", ty);
    if (types::bits_of(t) == 32) return state::scalar_type(e, is_signed ? "i32" : "u32", ty);
    return state::scalar_type(e, is_signed ? "i64" : "u64", ty);
}

static state::Ty pointer_to(state::Emitter *e, state::Ty *inner) {
    U32 space = 0;
    c::LLVMTypeRef address = c::LLVMPointerTypeInContext(e->context, space);
    state::Ty made = {
        .kind = {.pointer = {.element = inner, .address_space = space}}, .llvm = address, .name = "pointer"};
    return made;
}

// A slice, `str` or block (`[,]T`, `mem.alloc(T, [a, b])`'s) the checker names, when its element is a scalar, a record
// or an enumeration.
static Bool slice_of_checked(state::Emitter *e, types::TypeRef base, state::Ty *ty) {
    state::Ty character = {};
    if (base->kind == .text) {
        state::scalar_type(e, "char", &character);
        *ty = emit_memory::slice_type(e, character, "str");
        return true;
    }
    if (base->kind != .slice && base->kind != .block) return false;
    types::TypeRef element = types::element_of(base);
    state::Ty inner = {};
    Bool known = scalar_of_checked(e, element, &inner);
    known = known || (element->kind == .record && find_record_by_name(e, types::name_of(element), &inner));
    known = known || (element->kind == .enumeration && matching::type_enum(e, types::name_of(element), &inner));
    if (!known) return false;
    *ty = base->kind == .block ? emit_memory::block_type(e, inner, types::count_of(base))
                               : emit_memory::slice_type(e, inner, "slice");
    return true;
}

// The enumeration of another module that a payload names (`Result(usize, console.Error)`), declared when the type that
// holds it is first needed. Nothing for any other type, or an enumeration already declared.
static Str bare_name(Str name) {
    Usize start = 0;
    for (Usize i = 0; i + 1 < countof(name); i++)
        if (name[i] == ':' && name[i + 1] == ':') start = i + 2;
    return name[start:countof(name)];
}

static void ensure_enum(state::Emitter *e, types::TypeRef t) {
    if (t == nullptr || t->kind != .enumeration || e->options.checked == nullptr) return;
    state::Ty known = {};
    if (matching::type_enum(e, types::name_of(t), &known) ||
        matching::type_enum(e, bare_name(types::name_of(t)), &known))
        return;
    const types::Symbol *target = types::lookup(&e->options.checked->scopes, types::name_of(t));
    if (is_enum_symbol(target)) imported_enum(e, target);
}

// The checker's type `t` as a `Ty`, with `span` for an error. A chain of pointers and arrays is walked with a loop,
// then built from inside. `Void` (a function's result, what a pointer points at) is an LLVM `void`.
// `Result(T, E)` as the checker typed it: the two payloads, each with its enumeration declared first.
static state::TyResult result_from_checked(state::Emitter *e, types::TypeRef base) {
    ensure_enum(e, types::element_of(base));
    ensure_enum(e, types::error_of(base));
    state::TyResult ok = optional::payload_of_checked(e, types::element_of(base));
    if (ok == .error) return {.error = ok.error};
    state::TyResult bad = optional::payload_of_checked(e, types::error_of(base));
    if (bad == .error) return {.error = bad.error};
    return optional::build_result(e, ok.ok, bad.ok);
}

// The kinds of checked type that are not a scalar, a record or an enumeration: a vector (alone, not in a chain), an
// option, a result, a tuple, a function value or pointer; the error for the rest.
static state::TyResult other_from_checked(state::Emitter *e, types::TypeRef base, Bool alone, ast::Span span) {
    if (base->kind == .vector && alone) {
        state::Ty lane = {};
        types::TypeRef lane_type = types::element_of(base);
        if (scalar_of_checked(e, lane_type, &lane)) return vectors::make(e, lane, types::count_of(base));
    }
    if (base->kind == .option) {
        ensure_enum(e, types::element_of(base));
        return optional::from_checked(e, base);
    }
    if (base->kind == .result_type) return result_from_checked(e, base);
    if (base->kind == .tuple) return tupled::from_checked(e, base);
    if (base->kind == .fn_value) return lambdas::from_checked(e, base);
    if (base->kind == .function) return lambdas::pointer_from_checked(e, base); // a C function pointer
    Str shown = types::show(base);
    state::Error error = {.message = state::msg(format::push("not emitted yet: ", shown)), .span = span};
    state::free_text(shown);
    return {.error = error};
}

static state::TyResult type_from_checked(state::Emitter *e, types::TypeRef t, ast::Span span) {
    types::TypeRef chain[16];
    Usize depth = 0;
    types::TypeRef base = t;
    while (base->kind == .pointer || base->kind == .array) {
        if (depth == countof(chain)) return state::ty_fail("a type nested more than 16 deep", span);
        chain[depth] = base;
        depth += 1;
        types::TypeRef next = types::element_of(base);
        base = next;
    }
    state::Ty ty = {};
    Bool known = scalar_of_checked(e, base, &ty);
    if (!known && records::is_anonymous(base)) { // `struct { a: i32 }` as the checker names it: front::emit_record
        state::TyResult anonymous = records::from_checked(e, base, span);
        if (anonymous == .error) return anonymous;
        ty = anonymous.ok;
        known = true;
    }
    known = known || (base->kind == .record && find_record_by_name(e, types::name_of(base), &ty));
    known = known || (base->kind == .enumeration && matching::type_enum(e, types::name_of(base), &ty));
    if (!known && e->options.checked != nullptr && types::is_made(e->options.checked, base)) {
        // the `struct:` or `enum:` of a type function (`Pair(i32)`): built from the checker's type
        state::TyResult made =
            base->kind == .record ? records::from_made(e, base, span) : matching::enum_from_checked(e, base, span);
        if (made == .error) return made;
        ty = made.ok;
        known = true;
    }
    known = known ||
            (base->kind == .enumeration && matching::type_enum(e, bare_name(types::name_of(base)), &ty)); // imported
    // A C enumeration is its integer: the header's names are constants of it (`c::red`), never a type of the module.
    known = known || (base->kind == .enumeration && from_header(types::name_of(base)) &&
                      scalar_of_checked(e, types::element_of(base), &ty));
    known = known || slice_of_checked(e, base, &ty);
    if (!known && base->kind == .void_type) {
        ty = void_type(e);
        known = true;
    }
    if (!known) return other_from_checked(e, base, depth == 0, span);
    for (Usize i = depth; i > 0; i--) {
        types::TypeRef node = chain[i - 1];
        state::Ty *inner = own_type(e, ty);
        if (node->kind == .pointer) {
            ty = pointer_to(e, inner);
        } else {
            state::Ty made = {.kind = {.array = {.element = inner, .count = types::count_of(node)}},
                              .llvm = c::LLVMArrayType2(inner->llvm, types::count_of(node)),
                              .name = "array"};
            ty = made;
        }
    }
    return ty;
}

// A C union has the size and alignment of its biggest and most aligned member and no fields to name: it is made a
// struct of one array of integers as wide as the alignment (`struct sigaction` holds one, #2610), so a variable of it
// or of a struct that holds it is sized right and a C function can fill it.
static void make_c_union(c::LLVMTypeRef named, types::TypeRef base) {
    types::Target target = types::lp64();
    types::Layout size = types::layout(&target, base);
    if (!size.known || size.size == 0 || size.align == 0) return;
    U64 unit = size.align > 8 ? 8 : size.align;
    c::LLVMTypeRef lanes[1] = {nullptr};
    c::LLVMContextRef context = c::LLVMGetTypeContext(named);
    lanes[0] = c::LLVMArrayType2(c::LLVMIntTypeInContext(context, (U32)(unit * 8)), size.size / unit);
    c::LLVMStructSetBody(named, lanes, 1, 0);
}

static types::TypeRef unmade_c_record(state::Emitter *e, types::TypeRef t, Bool through_pointers);

// Names (as shells) the C records that `base` only points to, so its pointer fields have a type; `ensure_c_record`
// makes their fields when a type first names them.
static void name_pointees(state::Emitter *e, types::TypeRef base) {
    if (!types::is_complete(base) || types::is_union_record(base)) return;
    for (Usize i = 0; i < countof(types::slots_of(base).items); i++) {
        types::TypeRef pointee = unmade_c_record(e, types::slots_of(base).items[i].type, true);
        state::Ty known = {};
        if (pointee == nullptr || pointee == base || find_record_by_name(e, types::name_of(pointee), &known)) continue;
        char *label = state::cstr(types::name_of(pointee));
        c::LLVMTypeRef named = c::LLVMStructCreateNamed(e->context, label);
        mem::free(label);
        state::Ty ty = {.kind = .record, .llvm = named, .name = types::name_of(pointee)};
        emit_memory::add_record(e, (state::RecordType){.name = types::name_of(pointee), .ty = ty, .shell = true});
    }
}

// The members of a C union, read in place: each is at offset 0 of the array that sizes it. A member this emitter has
// no type for leaves the union without fields.
static void name_union_fields(state::Emitter *e, types::TypeRef base, Usize at) {
    Usize count = countof(types::slots_of(base).items);
    state::FieldInfo infos[:] = mem::alloc_slice(state::FieldInfo, count);
    ast::Span nowhere = {};
    for (Usize i = 0; i < count; i++) {
        types::TypeRef held = types::slots_of(base).items[i].type;
        state::TyResult made =
            held->kind == .fn_value ? lambdas::pointer_from_checked(e, held) : type_from_checked(e, held, nowhere);
        if (made == .error) {
            state::free_text(made.error.message);
            mem::free(infos.data);
            return;
        }
        infos[i] = (state::FieldInfo){.name = types::slots_of(base).items[i].name, .ty = made.ok};
    }
    e->records[at].fields = infos;
    e->records[at].overlay = true;
}

// A record that came from a C header (`c::FILE`): no declaration of the module made it, so it is made when a type
// first names it, with the fields the checker read. A field this emitter has no type for (a union, a function
// pointer) leaves the record opaque; a struct held by value is made first (`struct stat`'s `st_atim`, #2610): a pointer
// to it is still a pointer.
static void make_c_record(state::Emitter *e, types::TypeRef base) {
    Usize at = e->record_count;
    c::LLVMTypeRef named = nullptr;
    for (Usize i = 0; i < e->record_count; i++) {
        if (e->records[i].shell && state::same_text(e->records[i].name, types::name_of(base))) {
            at = i;
            named = e->records[i].ty.llvm;
            e->records[i].shell = false;
        }
    }
    if (named == nullptr) {
        char *label = state::cstr(types::name_of(base));
        named = c::LLVMStructCreateNamed(e->context, label);
        mem::free(label);
        state::Ty ty = {.kind = .record, .llvm = named, .name = types::name_of(base)};
        emit_memory::add_record(e, (state::RecordType){.name = types::name_of(base), .ty = ty});
    }
    name_pointees(e, base);
    Usize count = countof(types::slots_of(base).items);
    if (types::is_complete(base) && types::is_union_record(base) && count > 0) {
        make_c_union(named, base);
        name_union_fields(e, base, at);
        return;
    }
    if (!types::is_complete(base) || types::is_union_record(base) || count == 0 || count > 64) {
        return;
    }
    state::FieldInfo infos[:] = mem::alloc_slice(state::FieldInfo, count);
    c::LLVMTypeRef fields[64];
    ast::Span nowhere = {};
    for (Usize i = 0; i < count; i++) {
        // A function pointer of C is the bare `ptr` in the struct's layout, not a `fn` value's `{ code, context }`.
        types::TypeRef held = types::slots_of(base).items[i].type;
        state::TyResult made =
            held->kind == .fn_value ? lambdas::pointer_from_checked(e, held) : type_from_checked(e, held, nowhere);
        if (made == .error) {
            state::free_text(made.error.message);
            mem::free(infos.data);
            return;
        }
        infos[i] = (state::FieldInfo){.name = types::slots_of(base).items[i].name, .ty = made.ok};
        fields[i] = made.ok.llvm;
    }
    c::LLVMStructSetBody(named, fields, (U32)count, 0);
    e->records[at].fields = infos;
}

// The record at the bottom of a chain of pointers and arrays, when it is a C one that is not made yet.
static types::TypeRef unmade_c_record(state::Emitter *e, types::TypeRef t, Bool through_pointers) {
    types::TypeRef base = t;
    for (Usize guard = 0; guard < 16 && (base->kind == .array || (through_pointers && base->kind == .pointer));
         guard++) {
        types::TypeRef next = types::element_of(base);
        base = next;
    }
    Bool made = false;
    for (Usize i = 0; i < e->record_count; i++) {
        Bool open = e->records[i].shell && from_header(types::name_of(base));
        if (!open && state::same_text(e->records[i].name, types::name_of(base))) made = true;
    }
    if (base->kind == .record && !made && (from_header(types::name_of(base)) || in_module(types::name_of(base)))) {
        return base;
    }
    return nullptr;
}

// The first field held by value (a struct or an array of them) whose record is not made yet, else null.
static types::TypeRef unmade_field(state::Emitter *e, types::TypeRef record) {
    if (!types::is_complete(record) || types::is_union_record(record)) return nullptr;
    for (Usize i = 0; i < countof(types::slots_of(record).items); i++) {
        types::TypeRef inner = unmade_c_record(e, types::slots_of(record).items[i].type, false);
        if (inner != nullptr && inner != record) return inner;
    }
    return nullptr;
}

// Makes the C record at the bottom of `t`, the structs it holds by value first (`struct stat` holds three
// `struct timespec`, #2610): an explicit stack, since the emitter does not recurse.
static void ensure_c_record(state::Emitter *e, types::TypeRef t) {
    types::TypeRef pending[16];
    Usize top = 0;
    types::TypeRef first = unmade_c_record(e, t, true);
    if (first == nullptr) return;
    pending[0] = first;
    top = 1;
    while (top > 0) {
        types::TypeRef inner = unmade_field(e, pending[top - 1]);
        if (inner != nullptr && top < countof(pending)) {
            pending[top] = inner;
            top += 1;
            continue;
        }
        top -= 1;
        make_c_record(e, pending[top]);
    }
}

// A checker type as a `Ty` for the hook `state::type_of_checked`.
export state::TyResult type_of_checked(state::Emitter *e, types::TypeRef t, ast::Span span) {
    ensure_c_record(e, t);
    return type_from_checked(e, t, span);
}

// The checker's type of `x`, as a `Ty` (the hook `state::type_of_node`).
export state::TyResult type_of_node(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Expr *x) {
    Str kind = state::expr_kind_name(x);
    if (e->options.checked == nullptr)
        return state::ty_fail_with(
            x->span, "this needs the checker's types: none for the module, at an expression of kind `", kind, "`");
    types::TypeRef base = types::type_of(e->options.checked, x);
    if (base == nullptr)
        return state::ty_fail_with(x->span, "this needs the checker's types: the base type of an expression of kind `",
                                   kind, "` was not recorded");
    if (base->kind == .void_type) return state::ty_fail("not emitted yet: Void", x->span); // as before: no value
    return type_of_checked(e, base, x->span);
}

// `fpext` of an `f32`, or `sitofp` / `uitofp` of an integer the float's mantissa holds (24 bits for `f32`, 53 for
// `f64`: `i16`/`u16` and narrower to `f32`, `i32`/`u32` and narrower to `f64`). Null when `from` does not convert.
static c::LLVMValueRef float_conversion(state::Emitter *e, state::Value value, state::Ty to) {
    state::Ty from = value.ty;
    if (to.kind != .floating) return nullptr;
    if (from.kind == .floating) {
        if (state::width(to) > state::width(from)) return c::LLVMBuildFPExt(e->builder, value.llvm, to.llvm, "widen");
        return nullptr;
    }
    if (from.kind != .integer) return nullptr;
    U32 holds = state::width(to) == 16 ? 8 : (state::width(to) == 32 ? 16 : 32);
    if (state::width(from) > holds) return nullptr;
    if (state::is_signed(from)) return c::LLVMBuildSIToFP(e->builder, value.llvm, to.llvm, "convert");
    return c::LLVMBuildUIToFP(e->builder, value.llvm, to.llvm, "convert");
}

static Bool is_plain_integer(state::Ty t) {
    return t.kind == .integer;
}

static state::Status convert_failure(state::Value value, state::Ty to, ast::Span span, state::ConvertSite site) {
    if (site == .initialize) return state::failf(span, "initializing ", to.name, " with ", value.ty.name);
    if (site == .return_value)
        return state::failf(span, "returning ", value.ty.name, " from a function that returns ", to.name);
    return state::failf(span, "assigning ", value.ty.name, " to ", to.name);
}

// `value` as a `to`: as it is, a wider integer (the checker's widening rules: the same signedness, or unsigned to a
// strictly wider signed; none can fail, so no check), or an option's payload (`optional::wrap_some`).
// A function that takes a context first and drops it, calling `target` with the rest: the code of a `fn` value made
// from a function's name. One per function.
static c::LLVMValueRef function_thunk(state::Emitter *e, c::LLVMValueRef target) {
    Usize length = 0;
    const char *own = c::LLVMGetValueName2(target, &length);
    Str label = state::msg(format::push(own, ".thunk"));
    char *name = state::cstr(label);
    state::free_text(label);
    c::LLVMValueRef found = c::LLVMGetNamedFunction(e->module, name);
    if (found != nullptr) {
        mem::free(name);
        return found;
    }
    c::LLVMTypeRef inner = c::LLVMGlobalGetValueType(target);
    U32 count = c::LLVMCountParamTypes(inner);
    c::LLVMTypeRef given[65];
    c::LLVMTypeRef wrapped[65];
    if (count > 64) count = 64;
    c::LLVMGetParamTypes(inner, given);
    wrapped[0] = c::LLVMPointerTypeInContext(e->context, 0);
    for (U32 i = 0; i < count; i++)
        wrapped[i + 1] = given[i];
    c::LLVMTypeRef result = c::LLVMGetReturnType(inner);
    c::LLVMTypeRef outer = c::LLVMFunctionType(result, wrapped, count + 1, 0);
    c::LLVMValueRef thunk = c::LLVMAddFunction(e->module, name, outer);
    mem::free(name);
    c::LLVMSetLinkage(thunk, c::LLVMInternalLinkage);
    c::LLVMBuilderRef b = c::LLVMCreateBuilderInContext(e->context);
    c::LLVMPositionBuilderAtEnd(b, c::LLVMAppendBasicBlockInContext(e->context, thunk, "entry"));
    c::LLVMValueRef args[64];
    for (U32 i = 0; i < count; i++)
        args[i] = c::LLVMGetParam(thunk, i + 1);
    c::LLVMValueRef called = c::LLVMBuildCall2(b, inner, target, args, count, "");
    if (c::LLVMGetTypeKind(result) == c::LLVMVoidTypeKind)
        c::LLVMBuildRetVoid(b);
    else
        c::LLVMBuildRet(b, called);
    c::LLVMDisposeBuilder(b);
    return thunk;
}

static state::Status convert_value(state::Emitter *e, state::Value value, state::Ty to, ast::Span span,
                                   state::ConvertSite site) {
    if (state::same_type(value.ty, to)) {
        state::push_value(e, value);
        return state::success();
    }
    if (to.kind == .option) return optional::wrap_some(e, value, to, to.kind.option, span);
    if (to.kind == .result && value.ty.kind != .result) return optional::wrap_ok(e, value, to, to.kind.result, span);

    if ((to.kind == .slice || to.kind == .block) && value.ty.kind == .array)
        return emit_memory::array_value_as_slice(e, value, value.ty.kind.array, to);

    state::Ty from = value.ty;
    if (is_plain_integer(from) && is_plain_integer(to) && state::width(to) > state::width(from)) {
        Bool same_sign = state::is_signed(from) == state::is_signed(to);
        if (same_sign || (!state::is_signed(from) && state::is_signed(to))) {
            c::LLVMValueRef wide = state::is_signed(from) ? c::LLVMBuildSExt(e->builder, value.llvm, to.llvm, "widen")
                                                          : c::LLVMBuildZExt(e->builder, value.llvm, to.llvm, "widen");
            state::push_value(e, (state::Value){.llvm = wide, .ty = to});
            return state::success();
        }
    }
    if ((to.kind == .fn_value || to.kind == .fn_pointer) && from.kind == .pointer &&
        state::same_text(from.name, "null") && c::LLVMIsNull(value.llvm) != 0) {
        // `fix.set_loader(nullptr)`: no function, the zero of the parameter's type (#3036)
        state::push_value(e, (state::Value){.llvm = c::LLVMConstNull(to.llvm), .ty = to});
        return state::success();
    }
    if (to.kind == .fn_value && from.kind == .pointer && c::LLVMIsAFunction(value.llvm) != nullptr) {
        // The name of a function given to a `fn` parameter: a `fn` value is `{ code, context }` and its code takes the
        // context first, so the function is wrapped in a thunk that drops it.
        c::LLVMValueRef thunk = function_thunk(e, value.llvm);
        c::LLVMValueRef made = c::LLVMGetUndef(to.llvm);
        made = c::LLVMBuildInsertValue(e->builder, made, thunk, 0, "code");
        c::LLVMTypeRef word = c::LLVMPointerTypeInContext(e->context, 0);
        made = c::LLVMBuildInsertValue(e->builder, made, c::LLVMConstNull(word), 1, "context");
        state::push_value(e, (state::Value){.llvm = made, .ty = to});
        return state::success();
    }
    if (to.kind == .pointer && to.kind.pointer.element == nullptr && from.kind == .fn_value) {
        // A `fn` value given to a callback parameter of C: the bare code address.
        c::LLVMValueRef code = c::LLVMBuildExtractValue(e->builder, value.llvm, 0, "code");
        state::push_value(e, (state::Value){.llvm = code, .ty = to});
        return state::success();
    }
    c::LLVMValueRef floated = float_conversion(e, value, to);
    if (floated != nullptr) {
        state::push_value(e, (state::Value){.llvm = floated, .ty = to});
        return state::success();
    }
    return convert_failure(value, to, span, site);
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The module

// `let sin = m.sin` or `let Point = m.Point`: a name for a declaration of an imported module (#1714). The checker has
// typed it; there is nothing to emit, a call through it reaches the function itself.
static Bool is_module_alias(const state::Emitter *e, const ast::Decl *d) {
    if (e->options.checked == nullptr || d->kind != .variable || !d->kind.variable.is_new) return false;
    const ast::Expr *init = d->kind.variable.init;
    if (init != nullptr && init->kind == .type_value) return true; // `let Plain = fn(u64) -> u64`: the checker's alias
    if (init == nullptr) return false;
    if (init->kind == .name) {
        // a capitalized `let Word = c.Thing` or `Wide := u128`: the checker declared a type for the name
        const types::Symbol *own = types::lookup(&e->options.checked->scopes, d->kind.variable.name);
        return own != nullptr && own->kind == .type_name && own->decl == d;
    }
    if (init->kind != .member) return false;
    types::Names names = types::member_names(init);
    if (names.count < 2) return false;
    const types::Symbol *first = types::lookup(&e->options.checked->scopes, names.items[0]);
    if (first != nullptr && first->kind == .module_name) return true;
    // `let Allocator = c.SmithAllocator`: the checker declared a type for the name
    const types::Symbol *own = types::lookup(&e->options.checked->scopes, d->kind.variable.name);
    return own != nullptr && own->kind == .type_name && own->decl == d;
}

// `const Pair = (i32, f32)`: the checker declared a type for the name, with this declaration as its source. A `let Line
// = []u8` is skipped by the same test; there is no value to emit.
static Bool is_type_alias(const state::Emitter *e, const ast::Decl *d) {
    if (e->options.checked == nullptr || d->kind != .variable || !d->kind.variable.is_new) return false;
    if (d->kind.variable.init == nullptr) return false;
    const ast::Expr *init = d->kind.variable.init;
    if (init->kind != .tuple_lit && init->kind != .name && init->kind != .call) return false;
    const types::Symbol *symbol = types::lookup(&e->options.checked->scopes, d->kind.variable.name);
    return symbol != nullptr && symbol->kind == .type_name && symbol->decl == d;
}

// Pass 1: types, then every function and global. An error is kept and the walk goes on with the next declaration
// (#2982); a function that failed to declare is marked, so its body is not emitted.
static void declare_all(state::Emitter *e) {
    for (Usize i = 0; i < countof(e->tree->decls); i++)
        emit_memory::record_shell(e, e->tree->decls[i]);
    for (Usize i = 0; i < countof(e->tree->decls); i++) {
        const ast::Decl *d = e->tree->decls[i];
        if (d->kind == .record) state::collect(e, emit_memory::record_decl(e, d));
        if (d->kind == .enumeration) state::collect(e, matching::enum_decl(e, d));
    }
    for (Usize i = 0; i < countof(e->tree->decls); i++) {
        const ast::Decl *d = e->tree->decls[i];
        state::Status declared = state::success();
        if (d->kind == .function) {
            if (d->kind.function.body == nullptr)
                declared = call::prototype(e, d);
            else if (!is_template(d))
                declared = declare_function(e, d);
        } else if (d->kind == .variable) {
            continue; // after every function: a table of callbacks names functions declared below it (#2643)
        } else if (d->kind != .record && d->kind != .enumeration && d->kind != .import_module && d->kind != .import_c &&
                   d->kind != .import_from && d->kind != .static_assert_decl && d->kind != .asm_decl) {
            declared = state::not_emitted("this kind of declaration", d->span);
        }
        if (state::collect(e, declared)) state::skip_declaration(e, i);
    }
    for (Usize i = 0; i < countof(e->tree->decls); i++) {
        const ast::Decl *d = e->tree->decls[i];
        if (d->kind == .variable && !is_module_alias(e, d) && !is_type_alias(e, d))
            state::collect(e, emit_memory::global_variable(e, d));
    }
    if (e->options.checked != nullptr) {
        for (Usize i = 0; i < e->options.checked->instance_count; i++) {
            const types::Instance *instance = &e->options.checked->instances[i];
            state::Status declared =
                state::in_instance(state::in_module(declare_instance(e, instance), instance->prefix), i);
            if (state::collect(e, declared)) state::skip_declaration(e, countof(e->tree->decls) + i);
        }
    }
}

// A struct or array of numbers the evaluator built (#3039, baking), as the constant of type `to`: one LLVM constant,
// element by element in the order of the LLVM type's own elements. Nested structs, strings and pointers are not baked
// yet (false: the value is built at run time as before).
static Bool baked_aggregate(eval::Value v, state::Ty to, c::LLVMValueRef *out) {
    Usize count = eval::baked_cells(v);
    if (count == 0 || count > 65536) return false;
    builtin::Cells parts[:] = mem::alloc_slice(builtin::Cells, count);
    c::LLVMTypeRef kind = to.llvm;
    Bool is_array = c::LLVMGetTypeKind(kind) == c::LLVMArrayTypeKind;
    if (!is_array && c::LLVMCountStructElementTypes(kind) != count) {
        mem::free(parts.data);
        return false;
    }
    for (Usize i = 0; i < count; i++) {
        c::LLVMTypeRef part = is_array ? c::LLVMGetElementType(kind) : c::LLVMStructGetTypeAtIndex(kind, (U32)i);
        Bool is_float = false;
        U64 bits = 0;
        F64 real = 0.0;
        if (!eval::baked_cell(v, i, &is_float, &bits, &real)) {
            mem::free(parts.data);
            return false;
        }
        c::LLVMTypeKind part_kind = c::LLVMGetTypeKind(part);
        if (is_float && (part_kind == c::LLVMFloatTypeKind || part_kind == c::LLVMDoubleTypeKind)) {
            parts[i].item = c::LLVMConstReal(part, real);
        } else if (!is_float && part_kind == c::LLVMIntegerTypeKind) {
            parts[i].item = c::LLVMConstInt(part, bits, 0);
        } else {
            mem::free(parts.data);
            return false;
        }
    }
    c::LLVMValueRef *items = (c::LLVMValueRef *)parts.data;
    *out = is_array ? c::LLVMConstArray2(c::LLVMGetElementType(kind), items, count)
                    : c::LLVMConstNamedStruct(kind, items, (U32)count);
    mem::free(parts.data);
    return true;
}

// `x` built in a function nothing keeps and folded to the constant of type `to` (a global's initializer, #2510).
// The constant `front::eval` computes for `x` (#3039), as a number or a Bool of type `to`; false when it computes none
// of these, and the value is built and folded as before (a struct, a string: step 3).
static Bool computed_constant(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Expr *x, state::Ty to, c::LLVMValueRef *out) {
    if (e->options.checked == nullptr || e->instance != nullptr) return false;
    types::Checked *checked = (types::Checked *)(Usize)e->options.checked; // the evaluator reads names in its scopes
    eval::Outcome found = eval::value(checked, x);
    if (!found.known) return false;
    if (found.value == .aggregate && (to.kind == .array || to.kind == .record))
        return baked_aggregate(found.value, to, out);
    U64 bits = 0;
    if (found.value == .floating && to.kind == .floating) {
        *out = c::LLVMConstReal(to.llvm, found.value.floating.value);
        return true;
    }
    if ((to.kind != .integer && to.kind != .boolean) || !eval::bits(checked, x, &bits)) return false;
    if (found.value == .enumerator) return false;
    *out = c::LLVMConstInt(to.llvm, bits, 0);
    return true;
}

static state::Status fold_constant(state::Emitter *e, const ast::Expr *x, state::Ty to, c::LLVMValueRef *out) {
    if (computed_constant(e, x, to, out)) return state::success();
    if (to.kind == .array ||
        to.kind == .record) // a struct or array is written only when the evaluator computed it (#3039)
        return state::failf(x->span, "the initializer of a global is a constant of type ", to.name);
    c::LLVMTypeRef type = c::LLVMFunctionType(c::LLVMVoidTypeInContext(e->context), nullptr, 0, 0);
    c::LLVMValueRef scratch = c::LLVMAddFunction(e->module, ".fold", type);
    state::Ty none = {.llvm = c::LLVMVoidTypeInContext(e->context)};
    start_function(e, (state::FunctionInfo){.llvm = scratch, .llvm_type = type, .result = none});
    state::begin_scope(e);
    state::push_eval(e, x, state::hint_of(to));
    e->folding = true;
    state::Status ran = run(e);
    e->folding = false;
    state::Status result = ran;
    if (ran != .error) {
        state::Value value = state::pop_value(e);
        if (c::LLVMIsAConstantInt(value.llvm) == nullptr) {
            result = state::failf(x->span, "the initializer of a global is a constant known at compile time (", to.name,
                                  ")");
        } else if (state::same_type(value.ty, to)) {
            *out = value.llvm;
        } else { // the checker has accepted the width: a literal is built as an `i32` before it meets its field
            U64 bits = state::is_signed(value.ty) ? (U64)c::LLVMConstIntGetSExtValue(value.llvm)
                                                  : c::LLVMConstIntGetZExtValue(value.llvm);
            *out = c::LLVMConstInt(to.llvm, bits, 0);
        }
    }
    state::end_scope(e);
    c::LLVMDeleteFunction(scratch);
    return result;
}

// The `asm` literals of the module (D7, #2636), in order: LLVM module asm, which the object file's assembler reads.
static void append_module_asm(state::Emitter *e) {
    for (Usize i = 0; i < countof(e->tree->decls); i++) {
        const ast::Decl *d = e->tree->decls[i];
        if (d->kind != .asm_decl) continue;
        Str text = d->kind.asm_decl.text;
        c::LLVMAppendModuleInlineAsm(e->module, text.data, countof(text));
    }
}

// What a failed body leaves behind in the emitter: its open loops, defers and lambda frames (#2982). The half-built
// function stays in the module, which is not used once an error is kept.
static void recover(state::Emitter *e) {
    e->loop_count = 0;
    e->defer_count = 0;
    e->lambda_frame_count = 0;
    e->folding = false;
    e->instance_scope = "";
    e->instance = nullptr;
}

static void note_declaration(Str name) {
    Usize n = countof(name) < sizeof walk_declaration - 1 ? countof(name) : sizeof walk_declaration - 1;
    for (Usize i = 0; i < n; i++)
        walk_declaration[i] = name[i];
    walk_declaration[n] = 0;
    walk_kind = "";
}

[[std::c_name("front_emit_crash_declaration")]] export const char *crash_declaration_name() {
    return walk_declaration;
}

[[std::c_name("front_emit_crash_kind")]] export const char *crash_kind_name() {
    return walk_kind;
}

static state::Status emit_all(state::Emitter *e) {
    note_declaration("");
    try debug::begin_module(e);
    declare_all(e);
    Usize next = 0;
    for (Usize i = 0; i < countof(e->tree->decls); i++) {
        const ast::Decl *d = e->tree->decls[i];
        if (d->kind == .function && d->kind.function.body != nullptr && !is_template(d)) {
            if (d->kind == .function) note_declaration(d->kind.function.name);
            if (state::is_skipped(e, i)) continue;
            if (state::collect(e, emit_function(e, d, e->functions[next], nullptr))) recover(e);
            next += 1;
        }
    }
    if (e->options.checked != nullptr) {
        for (Usize i = 0; i < e->options.checked->instance_count; i++) {
            if (state::is_skipped(e, countof(e->tree->decls) + i)) continue;
            e->instance_scope = e->options.checked->instances[i].prefix;
            const ast::Decl *generic = e->options.checked->instances[i].decl;
            if (generic->kind == .function) note_declaration(generic->kind.function.name);
            state::Status emitted = emit_function(e, e->options.checked->instances[i].decl, e->functions[next],
                                                  &e->options.checked->instances[i]);
            e->instance_scope = "";
            emitted = state::in_instance(state::in_module(emitted, e->options.checked->instances[i].prefix), i);
            if (state::collect(e, emitted)) recover(e);
            next += 1;
        }
    }
    if (e->error_count > 0) return state::success(); // the module is not used: nothing more to build or verify
    append_module_asm(e);
    try debug::finish(e);
    try call::check_recursion(e->module);
    aggregates::lower(e->module); // a big struct or array lives in memory (#3058)
    char *problem = nullptr;
    if (c::LLVMVerifyModule(e->module, c::LLVMReturnStatusAction, &problem) != 0) {
        ast::Span nowhere = {};
        Str culprit = "";
        for (c::LLVMValueRef f = c::LLVMGetFirstFunction(e->module); f != nullptr && countof(culprit) == 0;
             f = c::LLVMGetNextFunction(f)) {
            if (c::LLVMCountBasicBlocks(f) > 0 && c::LLVMVerifyFunction(f, c::LLVMReturnStatusAction) != 0)
                culprit = state::msg(format::push(" (in ", (const char *)c::LLVMGetValueName(f), ")"));
        }
        state::Status failed = state::failf(nowhere, "LLVM rejects the module: ", (const char *)problem, culprit);
        c::LLVMDisposeMessage(problem);
        return failed;
    }
    c::LLVMDisposeMessage(problem);
    return state::success();
}

// The tree as an LLVM module in `context`, for `options.target`. The caller owns the context and disposes of the
// module. On an Error nothing is left behind: the half-built module is disposed of.
// Like `module`, but with every error the walk found, not the first: emit goes on past a failed declaration (#2982).
// With errors `module` is null; the caller frees each message and `errors.data`.
export Emitted module_all(c::LLVMContextRef context, const ast::Module *m, state::Options options) {
    char *name = state::cstr(m->file);
    char *triple = state::cstr(options.target.triple);
    c::LLVMModuleRef ir = c::LLVMModuleCreateWithNameInContext(name, context);
    c::LLVMSetTarget(ir, triple);
    state::Emitter e = {.context = context, .module = ir, .options = options, .tree = m};
    e.type_hook = type_of;
    e.node_type_hook = type_of_node;
    e.checked_type_hook = type_of_checked;
    e.convert_hook = convert_value;
    e.fold_hook = fold_constant;
    if (countof(options.target.data_layout) > 0) {
        char *layout = state::cstr(options.target.data_layout);
        c::LLVMSetDataLayout(ir, layout);
        e.target_data = c::LLVMCreateTargetData(layout);
        mem::free(layout);
    }
    mem::free(name);
    mem::free(triple);
    e.builder = c::LLVMCreateBuilderInContext(context);
    e.alloca_builder = c::LLVMCreateBuilderInContext(context);
    state::Status status = emit_all(&e);
    if (status == .error) state::add_error(&e, status.error);
    debug::release(&e);
    emit_memory::release(&e);
    matching::release(&e);
    c::LLVMDisposeBuilder(e.builder);
    c::LLVMDisposeBuilder(e.alloca_builder);
    if (e.target_data != nullptr) c::LLVMDisposeTargetData(e.target_data);
    for (Usize i = 0; i < e.function_count; i++) {
        state::free_text(e.functions[i].symbol);
        mem::free(e.functions[i].params.data);
    }
    mem::free(e.functions.data);
    mem::free(e.locals.data);
    mem::free(e.scope_marks.data);
    mem::free(e.work.data);
    mem::free(e.values.data);
    // B2's stacks: a loop or `defer` left open when another handler failed is still on them. Their last pop frees
    // them already, so this frees what is left; mem::free of null is nothing.
    mem::free(e.loops.data);
    mem::free(e.defers.data);
    mem::free(e.skipped.data);
    if (e.error_count > 0) {
        c::LLVMDisposeModule(ir);
        return (Emitted){.module = nullptr, .errors = e.errors[0:e.error_count]};
    }
    mem::free(e.errors.data);
    return (Emitted){.module = ir};
}

// The tree as an LLVM module, or its first error; `module_all` has every one.
export ModuleResult module(c::LLVMContextRef context, const ast::Module *m, state::Options options) {
    Emitted all = module_all(context, m, options);
    if (countof(all.errors) == 0) return all.module;
    for (Usize i = 1; i < countof(all.errors); i++)
        free_error(all.errors[i]);
    state::Error first = all.errors[0];
    mem::free(all.errors.data);
    return {.error = first};
}
